{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition","id":1167408,"title":"Replacing the Virtual Adepts and the Etherites with another Tradition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-13T14:04:08-08:00","id":1167408,"title":"Replacing the Virtual Adepts and the Etherites with another Tradition","content":"I recently ran a modern day game where several of my players expressed an interest in playing members of the Ahli\u2019Batin but also playing members of the Traditions, and not as double agents or dual Tradition/Craft Mages but fully Batini and fully council of Nine.<br /> <br /> So, I decided to say that the Batini never left the Trads (the other option was a council of 10 or 11 and I decided not to do that).<br /> <br /> Instead I chose to do something I\u2019d thought about a long time ago and create a new group, The Free Convenentions or FreeCons.<br /> <br /> I had toyed with this idea and formed it based on the idea of Technomancers who resisted the restructuring of the Order of Reason into the Technocracy back in the 19th century (there are many conflicting dates for when this actually happened) and the restructuring of the Technocracy again in the late 19th or early 20th century.<br /> <br /> These resistant technomancers didn\u2019t like the disolving of their convention or methodology or the new command structure and mission statement that they were forced to work under. While many of these individuals would have been unhappy but likely to just buckle under and many more would engage in minor acts of dissidence over the decades, some were actually unwilling to go along with this altogether.<br /> <br /> Now most of those people would have been assimilated back into the fold through conditioning, some would have been purged in the political infighting and personal rivalries that followed and others would have been forced into submission on pain of imprisonment or death (or worse) but some would have gone rogue <br /> <br /> While the various disparate individuals and factions would be far form capable of working together, the not so secret campaigns to force these rogues back into the fold may just have galvanized them into working together to some degree and, after years of ruthless warfare and numerous brutal deaths (largely on the side of the rogues), the individuals would have banded together and found themselves between a rock and a hard place, either stand alone against the forces of the Techoncratic Union, or submit to whatever fate the Union would allow them if they surrendered... or, join the Traditions.<br /> <br /> I really liked the idea and depicted the FreeCons as being a group of disparate technomancers with both a vision for a future that the Technocracy would not allow AND an appreciation of a cultural tradition that the Technocracy was hellbent on purging.<br /> <br /> I generally depict the FreeCons as being comprised of the Virtual Adepts, The Etherites, The Novalon (Harbingers of Avalon), The Dalou'laoshi/The Elemental Dragons (who according to Sydicate Revied have been largely purged), remnants of the Craft Masons and the Gabrielites/Cabal of Pure Thought as well some others who have formed a new convention within this Tradition. I also sometimes include the Solificati or Children of Knowledge and other groups as well.<br /> <br /> I have no ill will for the Etherites and VAs being a Tradition but I like this idea quite a bit and hope by sharing it that I stir up some suggestions on how ot flesh it out and hopefully improve it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-13T16:59:55-08:00","id":1167449,"title":"","content":"It's interesting, but I really don't like it. I feel the whole &quot;tech vs magic&quot; thing was such a 1st ed thing that the game has managed to move on from. I don't really see what having a Tradition Technocracy hybrid faction actually adds to the conflict.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-13T17:12:35-08:00","id":1167452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1167449#post1167449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's interesting, but I really don't like it. I feel the whole &amp;quot;tech vs magic&amp;quot; thing was such a 1st ed thing that the game has managed to move on from. I don't really see what having a Tradition Technocracy hybrid faction actually adds to the conflict.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well ion this case the FreeCons are actually a Tradition just like the VAs and the Etherites, it\u2019s a new vision for the former convention Traditions of the Council of Nine","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-13T17:50:09-08:00","id":1167464,"title":"","content":"There are also some timeline issues. These groups are getting shed at very different times. Some of the Order of Reason groups were already down and out well before the Union was formed and, considering the situations at the time, probably would have had a problem hanging around until the others showed up.<br /> <br /> Specifically, the Gabrielites were erased before the Union was formed. It seems more likely that the remnants would have had a much easier time rejoining their former brethren in the Chorus than in cooling their heels in the wilderness, dodging death squads, until The Electrodyne Engineers got pissy about the whole Ether thing.<br /> <br /> Multiply that a few times for the Craftmasons. They were holistically purged way back when. Their continued existence would more the stuff of Da Vinci Code-style conspiracy plots (and that's like having myths about secret masters held by the members of the Illuminati...)<br /> <br /> And so on....<br /> <br /> It seems like it would be more parsimonious to just have the Sons of Ether have been the vast majority of Electrodyne Engineers, but they took similarly situated buddies from the Progenitors and IBM and maybe a few (very few) from the other groups. (With the remaining Electrodyne Engineers getting folded into IBM and spurring the imminent change to It-X). Then, when the Virtual Adepts left the Union, they defected to the Sons of Ether and joined up as a sub-group of them. And the Sons of Ether (under whatever name pleases you) has been relatively open to Union defectors ever since. Which makes them a little untrustworthy to the other Trads. Since policing the former Unionists would pretty much require the Etherites to act like the Big Brother tactics that they were defecting from. Such an &quot;open arms(/closed eyes)&quot; stance has probably led to some very nasty infiltrations. The groups squeezed out before the whole Michelson-Morely debacle had to go it on their own (Templars), find safe harbor elsewhere (probably for the Gabrielites), or perished (most of them)....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 12-13-2017, 08:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-13T18:00:12-08:00","id":1167466,"title":"","content":"When the Technocracy reoorganizes as the Technocracy why couldn't the Traditions reorganize as a new faction? The Council of Mystic Traditions and Free Conventions? Honestly mage isn't hurt by having a 13 faction base or 7","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-13T18:17:47-08:00","id":1167472,"title":"","content":"For a private game, I don't really see a problem with keeping the Ahl-i-Batin in the Traditions, and the Society of Ether being replaced by a more general OoR/Technocracy defector Tradition. It's not that hard to reconcile the time-line stuff. The majority of defectors/purged before the Electrodyne Engineers did weren't organized enough to be their own faction, then a whole Convention defects and the earlier ones band together with them to form something bigger, etc.<br /> <br /> The bigger issue is actually how to handle the Disparate Alliance, since the Batini are a vital faction in binding them all together. Though that can easily happen with the Batini getting split when they were supposed to have left the Traditions, and the splinter faction being the one that doesn't trust the Traditions, even with Batini membership, to keep Nephandi influence down. <br /> <br /> Of course, there's lots of ways to redo the Traditions.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-13T22:37:17-08:00","id":1167524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1167464#post1167464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are also some timeline issues. These groups are getting shed at very different times. Some of the Order of Reason groups were already down and out well before the Union was formed and, considering the situations at the time, probably would have had a problem hanging around until the others showed up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I generally depict the various groups who originally left getting joined by various outcasts and rebels who tirckled in over the next century, some of which were fairly large at the time of their defection/dissolution.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1167464#post1167464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Specifically, the Gabrielites were erased before the Union was formed. It seems more likely that the remnants would have had a much easier time rejoining their former brethren in the Chorus than in cooling their heels in the wilderness, dodging death squads, until The Electrodyne Engineers got pissy about the whole Ether thing.<br /> <br /> Multiply that a few times for the Craftmasons. They were holistically purged way back when. Their continued existence would more the stuff of Da Vinci Code-style conspiracy plots (and that's like having myths about secret masters held by the members of the Illuminati...)</div> </div> </div> </div>I generally depict members of both the Gabrielites and Craftmasons as having survived and gone into hiding inside other conventions where their allies shielded them and provided refuge. As such, elements of both Conventions survived in secret well into the \u2018defection era\u2019.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1167464#post1167464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems like it would be more parsimonious to just have the Sons of Ether have been the vast majority of Electrodyne Engineers, but they took similarly situated buddies from the Progenitors and IBM and maybe a few (very few) from the other groups. (With the remaining Electrodyne Engineers getting folded into IBM and spurring the imminent change to It-X). Then, when the Virtual Adepts left the Union, they defected to the Sons of Ether and joined up as a sub-group of them. And the Sons of Ether (under whatever name pleases you) has been relatively open to Union defectors ever since. Which makes them a little untrustworthy to the other Trads. Since policing the former Unionists would pretty much require the Etherites to act like the Big Brother tactics that they were defecting from. Such an &amp;quot;open arms(/closed eyes)&amp;quot; stance has probably led to some very nasty infiltrations. The groups squeezed out before the whole Michelson-Morely debacle had to go it on their own (Templars), find safe harbor elsewhere (probably for the Gabrielites), or perished (most of them)....</div> </div> </div> </div>I can\u2019t disagree with this and must admit it\u2019s also an interesting take, I appreciate your contribution to the discussion and feel that this is a suggestion worth considering","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-13T22:40:52-08:00","id":1167526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1167472#post1167472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, there's lots of ways to redo the Traditions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn\u2019t mind hearing some of your ideas","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T02:45:34-08:00","id":1167552,"title":"","content":"Well, for me anyway, part of the problem with the Traditions (and a few other game's splats for that matter) is that there's generally two main styles of Tradition: &quot;Culture&quot; first Traditions that are organized around specific (generally) real world cultural practices, that might try to be more inclusive as times goes on but that first culture is always extremely dominant. &quot;Practice&quot; first Traditions that organized around specific goals for why you do what you do with magic.<br /> <br /> So one of the most direct ways of redoing the Traditions is picking one of those approaches and having all the Traditions follow that design.<br /> <br /> Everyone going Culture First means a lot more Traditions, with the nine seats on the Council (if you keep that concept) going to the current nine most politically powerful ones, or powerful alliances of them. You get things closer to the Fellowships from Dark Ages: Mage. This allows a lot more fluidity in the make up of the Council over time without having to have groups leave the Traditions altogether or get subsumed into other Traditions. This also helps avoid the oddity of some cultural groups getting split between 3-5 Traditions, while other Traditions end up having dozens of distinct cultural groups inside of them. This also makes those that go Disparate Craft a much more meaningful statement. Instead of, &quot;Well, we didn't feel like getting shoved into the Dreamspeakers, so we just went off to do our version of shamanistic practice on our own,&quot; you get things more like the Taftani and their, &quot;We refuse to submit to the rules of other mages, period.&quot;<br /> <br /> Everyone going Practice First makes it easier to condense the groups and down play (or even get rid of) the Crafts. In essence, you get something a bit closer to the Orders from Awakening, but more of them. These Traditions seek to recognize Mythic Threads that resonate with archetypal magic users, and let culture flavor their local variations. This does require a much rosier in-character founding of the Traditions where the Eurocentricism of the Hermetics, Chorus, and Verbena didn't mess everything up. Instead of the very Western Hermetics trying to gobble up all the high ritualist mages, they're simply the European flavor of the Tradition of High Ritual Magic, equal in standing respect as their counterparts from other areas of the world. Instead of all the variations of Hinduism somehow all ending up in the Chakravanti Tradition (with a few off-shoots), the Indian subcontinent would have a wide range of Traditions that have simply formed a relatively strong alliance around their local shared culture after long periods of external threats. From a more design perspective, this also lets you pick nine fundamental mythical archetypes that these practice focused Traditions are built around that have a much strong connection to the Spheres.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T05:37:42-08:00","id":1167581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zennis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1167524#post1167524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I generally depict the various groups who originally left getting joined by various outcasts and rebels who tirckled in over the next century, some of which were fairly large at the time of their defection/dissolution.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I generally depict members of both the Gabrielites and Craftmasons as having survived and gone into hiding inside other conventions where their allies shielded them and provided refuge. As such, elements of both Conventions survived in secret well into the \u2018defection era\u2019.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I can\u2019t disagree with this and must admit it\u2019s also an interesting take, I appreciate your contribution to the discussion and feel that this is a suggestion worth considering</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There is a qualitative difference between a large scale organized defection and being purged. The Craftmasons and Gabrielites didn't leave, peacefully or otherwise, they were killed off. The Sons of Ether and the Virtual Adepts aren't refugees, they're rebels and revolutionaries. It doesn't seem entirely plausible that the Craftmason remnants were waiting with open arms for the Gabrielites, then the Electrondyne Engineers, then the Analytical Reckoners.<br /> <br /> Sure, some of the Craftmasons may have made it out alive and found some group to take them in. (Interestingly the group that leaps to mind is the Batini because there is some significant overlap in some of the ways they do what they do. I'm putting the Hermetics to the side because, though they are really good at letting in people with ideas that can bend towards their core concept of magic. That's what Ex Misc is for. But they are also bastards who don't just hold grudges. They strap them to their backs so their hands are free to cast murderous spells of vengeance. And I can't see the old, powerful Houses forgetting the Craftmasons defection from the Order and, then.... Mistridge.) Considering the nature of their plight and the reach and resources of their primary adversaries in the High Guild, I just can't see a coherent organized Craftmason underground surviving Ksifirai assassins and a network of Gabrielite and High Guild informants that mirrors the extent of organized Christianity and the trade networks through 160 years of dedicated persecution and then waiting for another 70 years holed up with the remnants of their dire enemies and victimizers for an additional 80 years until the Eletrodyne Engineers defected. In fact, I think the major sticking point with this concept is the idea that the remnants of the Craftmasons wouldn't have just Cask of Amontillado-ed any Gabrielitse seeking succor.<br /> <br /> With the Gabrielites the situation is different. They did have a place to go. Even though they have significant bad blood with the Choristers, they do come from two factions within the Messianic Voices, so they have history. Moreover, that history is based on some concepts that make &quot;coming home&quot; a very powerful meme, the whole &quot;Prodigal Son&quot; thing. And the Chorus was the ecumenical, accepting side of the Messianic Voices. The remnant Gabrielites would be just another Voice added back into the Chorus, as it were. (And it may explain some of the reasons why the Chorus is depicted both as pretty happy, friendly gnositcs and stick-up-their-ass judgmental types.... It's the influence of the Cabal refugees who have bent the Chorus that way.) <br /> <br /> In either case, if those two groups did hide out with other Sects, don't forget the power of institutional thinking and adjustment to current circumstances. Once they've joined up and there's been about 6-8 generations worth of membership (for the Craftmasons) or 3-4 (for the Gabrielites), there aren't really enough folks (I'd say &quot;any&quot;, but these are Mages) who would think of themselves as being members of the Order of Reason (back when it was reasonable and not this thing it's become) to even see themselves as having much in common with the later disaffected groups. The students of the students of the students of the students of the students of a Craftmason purge survivor would think of themselves as Ahl-i-Batin first. (I mean, look at how all the groups that went into the soup pots of each Tradition have cohered.) <br /> <br /> Perhaps, riffing off the whole &quot;Sons of Ether&quot; as the core, they were actually active recruiters? If the Ahl-i-Batin are still visibly around, maybe the Etherites found out there was a faction or network of Batini that still oriented itself on more Craftmason-like principles and convinced them to join up. And sussed out some very Mind-oriented Choristers of Gabrielite lineages (though, really would the Etherites really WANT them considering their history with the Ivory Tower/NWO?). And even reached out to others, like House Verditus and Luxor in the Hermetics. Then they got the infusion of Virtual Adepts.... It would be a wild and wacky group (if you take out the ex-Gabrielites). But it wouldn't look all that different from the Etherites we have right now, just with more VR. And, oh, now they aren't just compromised, they are active poachers off the other Traditions, so their rep will take another significant hit. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T05:48:42-08:00","id":1167584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1167552#post1167552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, for me anyway, part of the problem with the Traditions (and a few other game's splats for that matter) is that there's generally two main styles of Tradition: &quot;Culture&quot; first Traditions that are organized around specific (generally) real world cultural practices, that might try to be more inclusive as times goes on but that first culture is always extremely dominant. &quot;Practice&quot; first Traditions that organized around specific goals for why you do what you do with magic.<br /> <br /> So one of the most direct ways of redoing the Traditions is picking one of those approaches and having all the Traditions follow that design.<br /> <br /> Everyone going Culture First means a lot more Traditions, with the nine seats on the Council (if you keep that concept) going to the current nine most politically powerful ones, or powerful alliances of them. You get things closer to the Fellowships from Dark Ages: Mage. This allows a lot more fluidity in the make up of the Council over time without having to have groups leave the Traditions altogether or get subsumed into other Traditions. This also helps avoid the oddity of some cultural groups getting split between 3-5 Traditions, while other Traditions end up having dozens of distinct cultural groups inside of them. This also makes those that go Disparate Craft a much more meaningful statement. Instead of, &quot;Well, we didn't feel like getting shoved into the Dreamspeakers, so we just went off to do our version of shamanistic practice on our own,&quot; you get things more like the Taftani and their, &quot;We refuse to submit to the rules of other mages, period.&quot;<br /> <br /> Everyone going Practice First makes it easier to condense the groups and down play (or even get rid of) the Crafts. In essence, you get something a bit closer to the Orders from Awakening, but more of them. These Traditions seek to recognize Mythic Threads that resonate with archetypal magic users, and let culture flavor their local variations. This does require a much rosier in-character founding of the Traditions where the Eurocentricism of the Hermetics, Chorus, and Verbena didn't mess everything up. Instead of the very Western Hermetics trying to gobble up all the high ritualist mages, they're simply the European flavor of the Tradition of High Ritual Magic, equal in standing respect as their counterparts from other areas of the world. Instead of all the variations of Hinduism somehow all ending up in the Chakravanti Tradition (with a few off-shoots), the Indian subcontinent would have a wide range of Traditions that have simply formed a relatively strong alliance around their local shared culture after long periods of external threats. From a more design perspective, this also lets you pick nine fundamental mythical archetypes that these practice focused Traditions are built around that have a much strong connection to the Spheres.</div> </div> </div> </div>This, to me, is beautiful as an alternative way to build out the whole mystico-political structure of Mage. Not that I don't love the glorious mess that it currently is and all the fun in trying to reconcile the various clash-y bits, but this might, in the end, make a more coherent, easier-to-grok and probably playable version of Mage. <br /> <br /> It does rely on &quot;the forest that is [definitely] being lost for the trees\u201d of M20. The &quot;Practice&quot;(-First) as a concept that binds the mages of a Sect together as fellow practitioners of magic all of whom have something in common in the way they do magic has been broken down into the individual Practices (sensu stricto in M20) of each individual mage. Without the now largely defunct concept of \u201cPractice\u201d(-First), the Sects in Mage, particularly in the Traditions, are really just political organizations whose members have that in common but their magic (as in \u201cHow they do it\u201d) can be relatively all over the place.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T09:16:34-08:00","id":1167672,"title":"","content":"I never had 1st edition, but wasn't the 1st edition origin of the Society of Ether completely independent of the Technocracy? They rose independently from a middle eastern group that penned the Kitab al-Alacir or something like that. If you went back to that being the case, you'd have a long standing technological Tradition ready to adopt those elements of the Technocracy that rebelled or were forced to flee.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T09:39:53-08:00","id":1167682,"title":"","content":"Hmm. <br /> <br /> Group One: The Nine Mystical Traditions, made up of the original nine, with the Ahl i Batin and Solificati still holding the seats of Connection and Matter, respectively. <br /> <br /> Group Two: The Technocratic Union of Universal Order, with the five Conventions, who are all pretty much totalitarian thugs.<br /> <br /> Group Three: The Secret Society of Free Reason, made up of the Electrodyne Engineers/Etherites, Virtual Adepts, Collectors of Light, Go Kamisori Gama, Harbingers of Avalon, Lightbringers who aren't willing to sign on to a doctrine of pure atheism, Aesclapians/Progenitors more interested in helping and healing than in creating a master race, Void Engineers who want to explore rather than sanitize, a few of the more science-oriented Children of Knowledge, and the handful of surviving Craftmasons who've been hiding in Russia or wherever. <br /> <br /> Group Four: The Confederation of Shadows, formed in the 19th century of the Knights Templar, Wu Lung, Bata'a, Children of Osiris, Hollow Ones, Sisters of Hippolyta, Lions of Zion, Children of Knowledge, and Ngoma, focused more on urban fantasy style mystic conspiracy and defending the mundane world from supernatural dangers than in the Ascension War. <br /> <br /> Such a thing might require certain alterations to mundane history in addition to mystic history, I suspect. But I think you could run a pretty fun game using group 3 and/or 4 with groups 1 and 2 being potential antagonists (or at least headaches) to the PCs goals. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T10:24:11-08:00","id":1167693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1167672#post1167672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never had 1st edition, but wasn't the 1st edition origin of the Society of Ether completely independent of the Technocracy? They rose independently from a middle eastern group that penned the Kitab al-Alacir or something like that. If you went back to that being the case, you'd have a long standing technological Tradition ready to adopt those elements of the Technocracy that rebelled or were forced to flee.</div> </div> </div> </div>Their origin mythology is present throughout the editions.<br /> <br /> While it does present them forming before joining the Order of Reason and the latter reshuffle into a Convention, that's true of pretty much all the founding groups of the Order of Reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T15:20:17-08:00","id":1167781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zennis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition#post1167408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These resistant technomancers didn\u2019t like the disolving of their convention or methodology or the new command structure and mission statement that they were forced to work under. While many of these individuals would have been unhappy but likely to just buckle under and many more would engage in minor acts of dissidence over the decades, some were actually unwilling to go along with this altogether.<br /> <br /> Now most of those people would have been assimilated back into the fold through conditioning, some would have been purged in the political infighting and personal rivalries that followed and others would have been forced into submission on pain of imprisonment or death (or worse) but some would have gone rogue</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't like Etherites much. They're made of a mesh-up steampunk aesthetic that might have worked as an alternative science methodology up to the fifties but that, in the modern world, they don't really seem to have a place any longer. No place considers that kind of science valid any longer and even if the works of Jules Verne might have kept it alive for a while it seems really out of place to me. Yes, there could still be some whack-o here or there but... not enough of them to actually be a Tradition, there simply isn't a recruiting base any longer.<br /> <br /> So, a different fringe science Tradition working against the Technocracy for their own reasons (like how the VA left it because of WW2) actually fits better in my book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T15:56:00-08:00","id":1167786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1167781#post1167781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't like Etherites much. They're made of a mesh-up steampunk aesthetic that might have worked as an alternative science methodology up to the fifties but that, in the modern world, they don't really seem to have a place any longer. No place considers that kind of science valid any longer and even if the works of Jules Verne might have kept it alive for a while it seems really out of place to me. Yes, there could still be some whack-o here or there but... not enough of them to actually be a Tradition, there simply isn't a recruiting base any longer.<br /> <br /> So, a different fringe science Tradition working against the Technocracy for their own reasons (like how the VA left it because of WW2) actually fits better in my book.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a rather restrictive view of them, though. While I agree that in many ways they are stuck in the past, they aren't <i>about</i> being stuck in the past. And most of those with a steampunk aesthetic are in on the joke. At their core, Etherites are about individual excellence, Science as a form of self expression, and things that are right because they are so elegant that dammit the universe really should work that way. They are famous for theories that have been left to decades gone by, but they themselves are not limited to those theories and can be just as cutting edge as any Convention.<br /> <br /> YMMV but to my mind Richard Feynman makes a pretty good template for a more modern Etherite.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T16:37:56-08:00","id":1167792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1167786#post1167786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a rather restrictive view of them, though. While I agree that in many ways they are stuck in the past, they aren't <i>about</i> being stuck in the past.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem, as far as I see it, is that they're stuck into the wrong kind of past. I mean, the Order of Hermes and the Akashayana are still teaching centuries-old rituals, yet they do not feel so out of place like the Etherites. Why? Because they're rooted into a specific subculture that it's still pretty much alive in the modern age. The vision of science, instead, is in the hand of the Technocracy and every scientist grows up thinking that what matters is to discover how reality works... I just can't see a breeding ground for SoE philosophy anymore.<br /> <br /> So yes, they were a tradition, but right now they just shouldn't have the numbers to be one. At least IMHO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T18:16:28-08:00","id":1167807,"title":"","content":"The thing that analysis overlooks, is that reality in Mage is subjective. Normal mundane science only works where the Technocracy has made it work as a method of introducing their vision of not science, but technology, to the masses. In the Mage universe what scientists study in school and then go out and apply in the field isn't actually discovering the truth of how the world works. It's discovering the mechanisms that the Technocracy wants them to find so that hypertech can transition to mundane tech.<br /> <br /> The Society of Ether's biggest draw is for all the scientists that Awaken and realize this and reject it on a fundamental philosophic level. The Etherites role if for people that want to apply the scientific method to a subjective reality. Their embrace of &quot;debunked&quot; theories, and flashy subcultures that idealize past eras of technology, is a statement of rejection of the Union's Time Table as being the true path of science. Being a steampunk ether-space train conductor is just as valid in Mage as being a spaceship pilot, and the Etherites want a world that acknowledges this instead of pursuing the Union's narrow view of science as a tool of controlling the course of human history. Because once you get past that, you can truly Science! the world of Mage as it really is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T03:45:05-08:00","id":1167859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1167807#post1167807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing that analysis overlooks, is that reality in Mage is subjective. Normal mundane science only works where the Technocracy has made it work as a method of introducing their vision of not science, but technology, to the masses.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know how Mage works, this is not the point.<br /> My point is that the modern age most popular &quot;debunked theories&quot; for science are something on the line of Chinese medicine, homeopathy, creationism or flat Earth, and they mostly do not fold into the Etherite paradigm. My point is that the alternative scientist of the modern age is more likely a kinesiologist doctor (that would join the Akashayana or eventually the Chakravanti) or a devoted creationist (more likely to join the Celestial Chours).<br /> <br /> Of course you still have a pro-Brontosaurus archeologist here and there but I really can't see the SoE being that many in the modern days... I see them better as orphans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T10:36:19-08:00","id":1167955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1167859#post1167859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know how Mage works, this is not the point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whether you know it or not, you're not applying that knowledge. Which is my point on why your point isn't convincing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My point is that the modern age most popular &quot;debunked theories&quot; for science are something on the line of Chinese medicine, homeopathy, creationism or flat Earth, and they mostly do not fold into the Etherite paradigm. </div> </div> </div>Everything folds into the Etherite paradigm. That's the whole point of it. SoE Revised <b>uses Chinese medicine to explain the difference between normal science and Science!</b>. The books literally take one of your examples to demonstrate how Ether science is performed compared to regular science. You're complaint isn't valid, because the books directly contradict it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My point is that the alternative scientist of the modern age is more likely a kinesiologist doctor (that would join the Akashayana or eventually the Chakravanti) or a devoted creationist (more likely to join the Celestial Chours). </div> </div> </div>This isn't how Etherite requirement works at all. The Etherites don't start with Sleepers that are already kooks by normal standards; they're usually too close-minded about their pet theories for standard recruitment and are prone to being Dissidents. Their preferred candidates are young minds still open to exploring the truth themselves instead of taking the school dictated textbooks and example experiments as vessels of truth. They don't want people already devoted to single theory (again, the Traditionbook has a section on the Etherite preference for polymaths in potential candidates because it denotes people more open to esoteric science than single-path students).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T11:22:10-08:00","id":1167970,"title":"","content":"My own personal history of the Sons of Ether (and yes, this will contradict material from &quot;canon&quot;) is that Aretus was an Awakened philosopher, mathematician, and engineer in the Hellenistic world of the 3rd century BC, who was expelled from the Architects of the Monolith (the ancient proto-Iteration X faction founded by Imhotep) for his heretical theories about AEther as the fundamental substance/energy that permeates all which exists and how one could manipulate it - and through it anything and everything - with the proper understanding and knowledge. (Aretus may or may not have been an alias/shadow name for Archimedes; Etherites continue to debate the subject.) Aretus's Book of the AEther, collecting his writings, teachings and theories, survived his death/disappearance, with copies showing up in Rome after the second Punic War and being known to (if not necessarily endorsed by) the Collegium Praecepti, as well as finding their way to the library of Alexandria, later to the Academy of Gondishapur and the Imperial Library of Constantinople and eventually to the House of Wisdom in Bagdad. It was here that members of the Ahl i Batin's University of Light translated it into it's Arabic form, the Kitab al'Athir.<br /> <br /> In the 12th century, Lorenzo Golo of the Hermetic House Verditius discovered a copy of the Kitab al'Athir and was inspired to use his newfound knowledge and theories to found his own house under the auspices of Ex Miscellania. At the same time, Simon de Laurent, a French veteran of the Second Crusade and member of the Knights Templar as well as somewhat disillusioned member of the Gabrielite Order of Pure Thought, has also found a copy of the original Greek version of the Book of AEther. The pair are put in touch with each other through a mutual acquaintance in House Jerboten, and after comparing notes and theories, both members abruptly abandoned their respective organizations with the intention of founding a completely new Fellowship. However, Golo is killed when his experimental airship explodes and Laurent is imprisoned by Gabrielite hardliners. (Some Etherite conspiracy theorists blame members of House Flambeau or Tytalus for Golo's death; some Hermetic historians believe the Tremere responsible but will not discuss it with outsiders.) Most of their handful of followers end up in Houses Verditius and Jerboton, or in the Craftmason's Fellowship, but a few remain independent and alone, passing on their knowledge and lore to a few apprentices.<br /> <br /> During the Enlightenment, a period when both the Mystic Traditions and the Order of Reason are fragmented and disorganized, there arise a number of &quot;natural philosophy guilds&quot;, small enlightened brotherhoods who draw inspiration and methods from the Kitab al'Athir/Book of the AEther in its various translations. These guilds - the Voltarian Order, the Knights of Golo, Filii Aether, Dues Spiritus, the Illuminated Acadamy, and others - gradually form their own network of correspondences, friendships and rivalries. All of this lays the ground work for the formation of the Electrodyne Engineers in the 19th century.<br /> <br /> In 1851, at the Great Exhibition in London, the Enlightened Society of Reason is formed from many of those groups evolved from the Order of Reason, as well as other unaligned Enlightened Scientists. While many members of the various natural philosopher guilds attend the Exhibition, many are wary (of not outright offended) by the Society's apparent focus on intellectual conformity and the use of science and technology to control society and civilization. Such ideas fly in the face of the philosophies of research, wonder, exploration and importance of individual inspiration espoused by Aretus and his Book of AEther. These Scientists form their own society, the Electrodyne Engineers. Active throughout the Victorian Era, the Engineers make contact with a number of Lodges connected to the Mystic Traditions, as well as with the Analytical Reckoners, a group even more repulsed by the Society's goals than the Engineers are.<br /> <br /> On the eve of the first World War, one of the leading Engineers of his generation, Andreas Vargo, in a desperate effort to halt the coming devastation, tries to take over Europe using his armada of Science(!) inspired airships and robot soldiers. He fails, and as a result, the Electrodyne Enginers as a whole are viewed as dangerous enemies to the Society's plans. Over the next few decades, the two groups wage a shadow war against each other. Knowing the Engineers need allies, Doc Eon, the Man of Infinite Tomorrows and paragon of his age, is able to negotiate an alliance with the Council of Nine Mystic Traditions, with the now christened Sons of Ether taking the long empty Seat of Matter as a full Tradition, and helping battle both the increasingly totalitarian Society (soon to be the Technocratic Union) and the Nephandi during WW2.<br /> <br /> As for the modern Sons of Ether, while a lot of them love the aesthetics and style of Steampunk, Art Deco Pulp, Silver Age Sci Fi, and Analog for their inventions (after all, what is the point of Science! if you can't do it with style?), their actual theories and inventions focus on Quantum Theory, Dark Matter/Dark Energy/Dark Fluid, Non-Euclidean Geometry, and other things which are quite frankly beyond my ability to grasp with any degree of understanding. But a lot of them also still like to fiddle around with things like atomic energy, miracle drugs, alternate realities, or trying to produce phlogiston, just because they can and it's fun.<br /> <br /> Such is how they are in my games, at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T12:46:48-08:00","id":1167994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1167955#post1167955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whether you know it or not, you're not applying that knowledge. Which is my point on why your point isn't convincing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not really here to convince you anyway, especially because you only answer to pick fights with someone. So, just like I once did, I won't consider you any longer for the remaining of this thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Your</i> complaint isn't valid, because the books directly contradict it. </div> </div> </div>This is a categorical syllogism: the fact that an Etherite might study alternative medicine doesn't make it an exclusive nor main Etherite discipline. It is, in fact, a field better suited to Akashayana and Euthanatoi rather than SoEs because of the spiritual ramifications. My observation is a matter of numbers and recruitment and not of what disciplines might eventually be covered by the Etherite paradigm; this is why your counter-argument has no relevance nor weight on what I wrote.<br /> <br /> But then again it doesn't really matter, feel free to use all the etherites you want in your campaigns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T15:04:18-08:00","id":1168029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1167994#post1167994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not really here to convince you anyway, especially because you only answer to pick fights with someone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, you you're going to complain about a syllogism in a post that opens with an ad hominem dismissal? Not really a great way to show that you've got something important to say here.<br /> <br /> While you're going to ignore me and all that, if you'd like to defend this statement as an actual observation instead of a person attack on me, please explain how posts #6,9, and 14 can be construed as attempts to pick fights with someone.<br /> <br /> You could also try to consider my statements in the light of trying to address what seems like a serious misunderstanding of the SoE in your posts, and my motivations might be an attempt to help show why what you're saying doesn't actually match what the books say; even if you don't get convinced, other people might value it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is a categorical syllogism: </div> </div> </div>Um... and? Categorical syllogisms are completely functional logical structures. This is a categorical syllogism:<br /> <br /> Users of the Onyx Path forums communicate by posting messages.<br /> Heavy Arms is a user of the Onyx Path forums.<br /> Heavy Arms communicates by posting messages.<br /> <br /> And... yep, that checks out as two true categorical premises and a logically sound conclusion. None of the formal syllogistic fallacies are present.<br /> <br /> Of course, my statement doesn't meet the formal criteria of a categorical syllogism (I didn't present any categorical premises to deduce a conclusion, I extrapolated from the texts and your posts to draw a conclusion).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the fact that an Etherite might study alternative medicine doesn't make it an exclusive nor main Etherite discipline. </div> </div> </div>Of course... the main Etherite discipline is how they study things, not specific field of study. An Etherite doesn't study traditional Chinese medicine exclusively, or modern medicine exclusively. They study both, and then they study each in the context of the other. The seek to expand their understanding of the totality of all medicine by not limiting themselves to the rules of one system of medicine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It is, in fact, a field better suited to Akashayana and Euthanatoi rather than SoEs because of the spiritual ramifications. </div> </div> </div>The idea that the Society of Ether doesn't study and use models of fields with spiritual ramifications is directly contradicted by the text. Understanding spiritual ramifications in Chinese medicine is as important to an Etherite as it is for understanding biological complications in modern medicine; aka very important. Only by fully understanding Chinese medicine in its own context - because reality is subjective and everything exists are fundamental to Etherite paradigm - can an Etherite translate that understanding towards their greater understanding of all medicine (applying Life magic to heal people).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My observation is a matter of numbers and recruitment and not of what disciplines might eventually be covered by the Etherite paradigm; this is why your counter-argument has no relevance nor weight on what I wrote. </div> </div> </div>So... how many disillusioned young academics and scientists are out there that feel stifled by modern scientific bureaucracy and are looking for the mentorship of someone that shares their desires to discover deeper truths about the universe instead of sitting in a lab for a decade doing analysis for someone else's pet theory?<br /> <br /> How many people are studying traditional Chinese medicine in order to practice it professionally?<br /> <br /> Because the first are the primary recruits for the SoEs, not the second... and while I'm not sure how you'd manage to actually answer those questions, there's clearly more than enough of people from group A for the Tradition to recruit from.<br /> <br /> If anything, the Etherites are more relevant than ever, because they have the best appeal to every millennial with a college degree in STEM or social scienes, and is currently working a retail (or whatever equally unsatisfying) job. We have a whole generation of people that (a) are highly disappointed with a system of education and employment that's failed them, (b) generally value experience over material gain, and (c) rather open to sub-culture based fashion statements as group identifiers (there's a lot of steampunk enthusiasts out there right now that were born after 1982). The US is basically the perfect breeding ground for Etherites right now.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T17:57:07-08:00","id":1168064,"title":"","content":"Oh, um, I just wanted to mention that Society of Ether isn't just made up of steampunks who really dig Jules Verne. They also got atompunks who really dig Star Trek, Flash Gordon and Robert Heinlein. <br /> <br /> Just saying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T18:09:48-08:00","id":1168069,"title":"","content":"I believe one of the pre-made character templates in the original Sons of Ether Tradition Book was a Metaphysician who worked with biofeedback and other methods (some of which are accepted as legitimate therapeutic and medical activities) to promote a holistic version of scientific (or would that be &quot;Scientific!&quot;?) mental and physical health. <br /> <br /> Perhaps ironically, the two best examples I can think of of potential inspirations for Mage characters who hold a largely scientific world view but still engage in alternative medicinal practices (mind-body intervention and homeopathy, respectively) - the main characters in Dean Koontz's <b>Demon Seed</b> and Scarlett Thomas's <b>PopCo</b> - both feel more suited to the <i>Virtual Adepts</i> than anyone else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T18:27:44-08:00","id":1168075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weirdboyz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1168064#post1168064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, um, I just wanted to mention that Society of Ether isn't just made up of steampunks who really dig Jules Verne. They also got atompunks who really dig Star Trek, Flash Gordon and Robert Heinlein.<br /> <br /> Just saying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are cool. I also like Diesel Punk ones, taking inspiration from German Expressionism, Film Noir and WW2 military designs, especially when it comes to making ones who are hardcore Ascension Warriors of Central or Eastern European lineage. And New Wave Science! types in the vein of Buckaroo Banzai. Anime Otaku are fun too. <br /> <br /> But then, I once made a Science Diva whose personality was based on Rarity from My Little Pony, so I'm clearly very, very weird.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T18:45:04-08:00","id":1168085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1168075#post1168075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Those are cool. I also like Diesel Punk ones, taking inspiration from German Expressionism, Film Noir and WW2 military designs, especially when it comes to making ones who are hardcore Ascension Warriors of Central or Eastern European lineage. And New Wave Science! types in the vein of Buckaroo Banzai. Anime Otaku are fun too.<br /> <br /> But then, I once made a Science Diva whose personality was based on Rarity from My Little Pony, so I'm clearly very, very weird.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honestly, given the huge amount of sci-fi we we've got these days with shows like Doctor Who, Stranger Things, Fringe, Sense8 and a shit-ton of superhero stuff like the Flash, Ant-Man, Iron Man, and others I really feel like the Society of Ether would not lack for people inspired by really, really weird science that defies Technocratic convention. While all the examples I listed may be light on Science they still all capture, in their own ways, the root ethos/paradigm of the the Society of Ether, which is anything is anything is possible in a subjective universe so why not allow yourself to be awesome? <br /> <br /> Also, I love your Space Diva concept. Keep being awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T18:52:57-08:00","id":1168088,"title":"","content":"If you asked my to sum up the Etherites in a single idea, it would be that these are people who look at various things from science, engineering and technology with a sense of wonder, saying, &quot;Wow, that's really cool. Now let's Ether it up and make it <i>20% MORE AWESOME</i>!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T12:22:57-08:00","id":1168591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1167466#post1167466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When the Technocracy reoorganizes as the Technocracy why couldn't the Traditions reorganize as a new faction? The Council of Mystic Traditions and Free Conventions? Honestly mage isn't hurt by having a 13 faction base or 7</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yes that's a problem. At the root of all this, there is mystic belief. The Traditions cannot be more or less than 9. They can only by 9 (that is why the appearance of the 10th seat is so problematic). For what reason ? Because nine is a mystic number. Actually, nine is the most mystic number of Mages ^^ and it is present in many references. This is canon, and of course you could chose to do otherwise. However, it is at the roots of the game. I'm just explaining why it is this way in the official setting. Several clarifications :<br /> - In numerology, nine is the number of Magic (this would I think the first reason for the authors to choose this number),<br /> - It is a sacred number, symbol of wisdom and fullfilment,<br /> - It's the number of heaven,<br /> - In hinduism, it is the number of Brahma, the Creator<br /> - In China, the ninth day of the New Year is the birth of the Jade Emperor (In Taoism, the Jade Emperor is divine),<br /> - For the Hebrews, nine is the number of truth,<br /> - In Tarot, nine is the number of the Hermit, symbol of accomplishment. He is the figure of the one that has reached Ascension to enlighten others,<br /> You can also read this source for other explanations and the importance of this number in various religions and beliefs : <a href=\"http://www.thehindu.com/life-and-style/the-mystical-number-nine/article2514648.ece\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.thehindu.com/life-and-sty...cle2514648.ece</a><br /> <br /> Concerning the VA and the SoE, they are part of the Traditions not because of mere happenstence. They were not just here at the right time. They surely are Technomancers, but they really are Mystic Traditions too. Take the VA for exemple. Both Iteration X and VA want to transcend humanity. While the former try to reach that goal by merging with the Machine, the latter is pursuing a mystical ascension by freeing the spirit from the body to reach a new (virtual) reality. Their objective is fundamentally opposed and that mystical belief is why the VA's place is with the Traditions and not the Technocracy. Same is true with the Etherites. There is mystical belief in the Ether. It is substance that could move forces, light and matter. Ether is a primordial god in the Greek mythology personifying celestial forces and their brithness. Well, this is the Force from Star Wars in a way ! Definitely mystic ^^<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1167792#post1167792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem, as far as I see it, is that they're stuck into the wrong kind of past. I mean, the Order of Hermes and the Akashayana are still teaching centuries-old rituals, yet they do not feel so out of place like the Etherites. Why? Because they're rooted into a specific subculture that it's still pretty much alive in the modern age. The vision of science, instead, is in the hand of the Technocracy and every scientist grows up thinking that what matters is to discover how reality works... I just can't see a breeding ground for SoE philosophy anymore.<br /> <br /> So yes, they were a tradition, but right now they just shouldn't have the numbers to be one. At least IMHO.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are still fields in Physics that defy the existing laws. Physicians are still searching a way to make Physics work by pursuing the dream of Unity (Grand Unification Theory). There is plenty of place for the SoE ! Quantum mechanics to say the least !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T12:49:32-08:00","id":1168609,"title":"","content":"Apparently zero point energy has been described in some circles as a kind of reintroduction of aether to physics, so make of that what you will.<br /> <br /> Edit: As for the number nine, it's also the Norse number of worlds/realms, and in Christianity is seen as a trinity of trinities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T23:59:16-08:00","id":1168730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1168609#post1168609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apparently zero point energy has been described in some circles as a kind of reintroduction of aether to physics, so make of that what you will.</div> </div> </div> </div>The books (I believe it was the SoE trad books) also put forth the idea that Dark Matter is just the new name for Ether. And that by allowing it to enter the Consensus, the Void Engineers have tacitly admitted what the Etherites have been saying all along.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T05:36:56-08:00","id":1168776,"title":"","content":"Well.... The Nine Traditons, historically, haven't been. So, if HAS to be 9, then the Traditions aren't it. Typically the number is 8. Seats are not occupied for centuries at a time. The Solificati slunk away almost right after the Convocation.and there aren't any real contenders to sit in the Seat of Matter for a very long time. The number did jump back to 9 for the decades after the Etherites joined up. But then the Batini didn't so much tip over the table and leave in a huff as they just stopped showing up in such a subtle way that it really took awhile for everyone to catch on that no one had been sitting in the Seat of Correspondence for a while. The whole &quot;NINE Traditions&quot; thing was 1457-1470, 1904 - 1922 &amp; 1961 onwards. That's roughly 80 total years out of 550. <br /> <br /> So, taking a bunch of random factoids from various places doesn't pan out on the ground. It seems more like post hoc rationales tacked onto, perhaps, the Order of Hermes putting their particular take on that out there. (Perhaps, once Baldric La Salle realized he wasn't going to be adding a slew of new Houses, he went for the &quot;The Order of Hermes started with 9 and that was a good number. so let's do that&quot; but, even then, that seems like adding significance to something circumstantia from seven centuries beforehand. It could have been 8 Houses if Tremere and Tytalus's Master had pushed for her own House with her apprentices in place instead of setting them up on their own. Or 10, if Trianoma hadn't stepped back into Bonisagus's shadow. Or 7/8 if Diedne had told the Order to go screw themselves because they didn't need to join their little club. And so on.) <br /> <br /> Also, if we are going to play numerological games, it has been put out there in the material more than once that the number 9 is also seen as being incomplete. Ten is 1 is Unity. The Nine Traditions mystically have always been pining for that 10th Seat, 10th Sphere, 10th member of the family.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T05:42:22-08:00","id":1168778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1168730#post1168730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The books (I believe it was the SoE trad books) also put forth the idea that Dark Matter is just the new name for Ether. And that by allowing it to enter the Consensus, the Void Engineers have tacitly admitted what the Etherites have been saying all along.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Seems like the Union has always had a problem with that &quot;special something&quot; that underlies everything. They always had a Prime Sphere to deal with and they just seem to be putting various definitions of exactly what that is fly without any real coherency. They definitely said &quot;No&quot; unequivocally to Ether, but it's really not that easy to reconcile how the Syndicate handles concept of value and worth with the same thing that Iteration X looks at and thinks of something as tangible as &quot;fuel&quot; in one sense or another. I don't think the VE's holding up their hands and saying &quot;Dark Matter(/Energy)&quot; is going to resolve the matter to anyone's satisfaction, probably not even their own very much. (The scale and way those things work isn't really applicable to their issues at hand.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T10:36:45-08:00","id":1168845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1168778#post1168778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Seems like the Union has always had a problem with that &quot;special something&quot; that underlies everything. They always had a Prime Sphere to deal with and they just seem to be putting various definitions of exactly what that is fly without any real coherency. They definitely said &quot;No&quot; unequivocally to Ether, but it's really not that easy to reconcile how the Syndicate handles concept of value and worth with the same thing that Iteration X looks at and thinks of something as tangible as &quot;fuel&quot; in one sense or another. I don't think the VE's holding up their hands and saying &quot;Dark Matter(/Energy)&quot; is going to resolve the matter to anyone's satisfaction, probably not even their own very much. (The scale and way those things work isn't really applicable to their issues at hand.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, it doesn't matter if anyone makes anything of Dark Matter within the Technocracy. The Etherites simply claim that its inclusion in the Consensus is an admission of having been wrong, for no other reason than because it makes the Etherites feel smug and validated after over a century of their way of thinking being marginalized. No one ever said the Ascension War couldn't be petty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T12:22:54-08:00","id":1168883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1168776#post1168776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well.... The Nine Traditons, historically, haven't been. So, if HAS to be 9, then the Traditions aren't it. Typically the number is 8. Seats are not occupied for centuries at a time. The Solificati slunk away almost right after the Convocation.and there aren't any real contenders to sit in the Seat of Matter for a very long time. The number did jump back to 9 for the decades after the Etherites joined up. But then the Batini didn't so much tip over the table and leave in a huff as they just stopped showing up in such a subtle way that it really took awhile for everyone to catch on that no one had been sitting in the Seat of Correspondence for a while. The whole &quot;NINE Traditions&quot; thing was 1457-1470, 1904 - 1922 &amp; 1961 onwards. That's roughly 80 total years out of 550.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not because they did not manage to remain nine that the Concil of the Nine Mystic Traditions did not intend to be nine. They even continued calling themselves that way though, as you said, they were not actually nine. They forged a Mystic alliance. It's even in their name. The betrayal of Teomim is a failure they suffered for centuries. The Council not being complete is one of their weakness. It is not only a practical one (well they lacked numbers) it's also a mystical and a spiritual one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1168776#post1168776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, taking a bunch of random factoids from various places doesn't pan out on the ground.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not random. This comes from various beliefs all other the world. These &quot;random factoids&quot; are the core of Mage: The Ascension. I could have missed your point or you misunderstood something of the game. Please, could you clarify ?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1168776#post1168776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems more like post hoc rationales tacked onto, perhaps, the Order of Hermes putting their particular take on that out there. (Perhaps, once Baldric La Salle realized he wasn't going to be adding a slew of new Houses, he went for the &quot;The Order of Hermes started with 9 and that was a good number. so let's do that&quot; but, even then, that seems like adding significance to something circumstantia from seven centuries beforehand.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Order of Hermes is the best example when justifying my point. They even forced the other Traditions to adopt the Nine Spheres of Magick. Nine is not a random number as I said nor, &quot;a good number&quot; as you put it. It is not circumstantial either. Numerology exists in many beliefs and share some common ground. The Hermetics are partly responsible for that since part of their initial belief comes from the Jewish Kabbalah, itself present in many other beliefs. It makes the magick of the Order, the &quot;new root of magick&quot; in some way (not sure if I made myself clear with that... I could complete it later if need be).[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1168776#post1168776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, if we are going to play numerological games, it has been put out there in the material more than once that the number 9 is also seen as being incomplete. Ten is 1 is Unity. The Nine Traditions mystically have always been pining for that 10th Seat, 10th Sphere, 10th member of the family.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not a numerological game. We're discussing the cosmogony of Mages. Hardly a game for them (we're not talking personnal beliefs outside of Mages of course... Still a RPG ^^). As I said, numerology is central in many beliefs.<br /> <br /> And yes, 10 is Unity. It completes the circle. It's the ultimate goal for many Mages. That is why the number nine is so important and that is why the appearance of the 10th seat was so extraordinary. It brought their mystical belief to a whole new level. It justified their mysticism and it acted like a proof that they were on the right path to Ascension. When Judgement is coming, the 10th Sphere will reveal itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T17:11:07-08:00","id":1168953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1168845#post1168845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, it doesn't matter if anyone makes anything of Dark Matter within the Technocracy. The Etherites simply claim that its inclusion in the Consensus is an admission of having been wrong, for no other reason than because it makes the Etherites feel smug and validated after over a century of their way of thinking being marginalized. No one ever said the Ascension War couldn't be petty.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it's only petty if the Ether dispute was over a pet theory rather than an entire approach to science (or Science, as the case may be). Calling it another form of Ether may be pointless and petty, but if a Convention is appealing to a vast, undetectable cosmic substance in order to make sure that the universe behaves in an elegant and relateable way it means the Society's way of thinking is still embedded in the Union. That doesn't just feel good, that is a victory.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T17:44:14-08:00","id":1168959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1168953#post1168953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well it's only petty if the Ether dispute was over a pet theory rather than an entire approach to science (or Science, as the case may be). Calling it another form of Ether may be pointless and petty, but if a Convention is appealing to a vast, undetectable cosmic substance in order to make sure that the universe behaves in an elegant and relateable way it means the Society's way of thinking is still embedded in the Union. That doesn't just feel good, that is a victory.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also a larger blow against the Union's more general goal of trying to codify every aspect of Reality in the Consensus. Even now, no one <i>really</i> knows what Dark Matter is. Scientists (at least the Sleeper ones) only knew to look for it at all because the mass equation for the known universe were off. Thus, in WoD, we have a situation where the Union has been forced to admit on the public scale that there are some things Science does not understand. That the universe is still mysterious as hell. That there are gaps in scientific understanding; blank edges to the map.<br /> <br /> Which is where the Traditions come in, ready to capitalize on that by writing &quot;Here Be Dragons&quot; again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T18:20:05-08:00","id":1168969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NicoTheDuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1168883#post1168883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not because they did not manage to remain nine that the Concil of the Nine Mystic Traditions did not intend to be nine. They even continued calling themselves that way though, as you said, they were not actually nine. They forged a Mystic alliance. It's even in their name. The betrayal of Teomim is a failure they suffered for centuries. The Council not being complete is one of their weakness. It is not only a practical one (well they lacked numbers) it's also a mystical and a spiritual one.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This is not random. This comes from various beliefs all other the world. These &quot;random factoids&quot; are the core of Mage: The Ascension. I could have missed your point or you misunderstood something of the game. Please, could you clarify ?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Order of Hermes is the best example when justifying my point. They even forced the other Traditions to adopt the Nine Spheres of Magick. Nine is not a random number as I said nor, &quot;a good number&quot; as you put it. It is not circumstantial either. Numerology exists in many beliefs and share some common ground. The Hermetics are partly responsible for that since part of their initial belief comes from the Jewish Kabbalah, itself present in many other beliefs. It makes the magick of the Order, the &quot;new root of magick&quot; in some way (not sure if I made myself clear with that... I could complete it later if need be).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This is not a numerological game. We're discussing the cosmogony of Mages. Hardly a game for them (we're not talking personnal beliefs outside of Mages of course... Still a RPG ^^). As I said, numerology is central in many beliefs.<br /> <br /> And yes, 10 is Unity. It completes the circle. It's the ultimate goal for many Mages. That is why the number nine is so important and that is why the appearance of the 10th seat was so extraordinary. It brought their mystical belief to a whole new level. It justified their mysticism and it acted like a proof that they were on the right path to Ascension. When Judgement is coming, the 10th Sphere will reveal itself.[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> It's precisely a numerological game. And it's being played by the developers as much as it's being played by the historical actors in the world of mage. The fact you can grab a number of different factoid from various unrelated mystical traditions (small &quot;t&quot;) from around the world doesn't actually prove your point. Some of them are used in context with material as presented in the game. Those might work. But they are suspect as they aren't attributed to the Convocation per se. They are pretty much post hoc, justifying what they have decide is important NOW. It's like watching people play the same number games with the Great Pyramid. It's attributing meaning because it's important to the person making the assertion, even though it doesn't have any relevance to that which the meaning is being attributed to. Numerology exists, sure. But the number Nine as it is important to many branches of modern paganism, the way it has been important to different interpretations of the Kabbalah and so on.... there's nothing consistent across cultures about the meaning. Particularly not the ones you are attributing to it. <br /> <br /> And agreeing with the last bit shows that, fundamentally, the number 9 is no more or less important than 10. If 9 is all important, 10 can't be. If 10 is the goal, then it's not 9. Backed up fundamentally by the fact that, if 9 is really all that important and so utterly fundamental, then it really can't be 8 when it's not 9 and that's okay. If 9 is this mystic tie that binds, then they would need to grab ANYONE relevant to sit in that Seat or undermine the foundation of their actual existence. Anyone relevant. Grab on to the Solificati with both hands and make them stay. Fission off some sub-group (probably a House) and upgrade them to Tradition status to take the seat. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T05:09:49-08:00","id":1171770,"title":"","content":"The only way that 9 is relevant is the extent to which the Traditions have chosen to organize themselves according to the nine Spheres \u2014 a notion that M20 has severely downplayed, but not quite removed. <br /> <br /> As they're presented in their Revised Tradition Book, the Sons of Ether could be merged with the VAs and hardly anyone would notice \u2014 especially now that cyberpunk (the basis of the VAs) has arguably turned out to be \u201csci-fi of the 90s\u201d, putting it in the same boat as the various retrotechs that so many Etherites dabble in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T10:15:12-08:00","id":1171823,"title":"","content":"While I don't think retconning in a merger is hard to do, having them merge in the &quot;now&quot; of the setting would be a fairly bigger deal compared to having them always been that way as initially suggested.<br /> <br /> One of the big reasons is what I generally refer to the &quot;scientist vs. engineer&quot; split. The predominant mentality of the Etherites is science. That is, the rational expansion of their understanding of the universe, from which they can create functional models, from which they can do stuff. The predominant mentality of the Adepts is engineering. They take an existing model, and expand that, and themselves, and then what they can do, with it.<br /> <br /> Asking the VAs to operate in the SoE's academia and formalities would be very difficult. Asking the SoE's to operate in the VA's individualistic and anachristic social structures would likewise not work well. Neither group is going to react to, &quot;The Ahl-i-Batin want back in, so make room and combine,&quot; well, and would probably both respond with, &quot;they're religious mages, why don't they just join the Chorus. The Chorus could use some better representation in their ranks from the Arab world anyway.&quot;<br /> <br /> It also presupposes that the Virtual Adepts aren't going to evolve with the times as younger Adepts adjust their technology to what's cutting edge now instead of what was cutting edge 20 years ago. The idea that the cyberpunk genre is so firmly rooted in the 80s that a group inspired by it can't be adapted to confront the technological realities of the 21st century is kind of ridiculous as the genre has itself updated and adapted up until this day. Not every cyberpunk genre piece goes for the retro style of the late 80s and early 90s There's also plenty of genre entries that hold up today with minimal alterations (ex: Ghost in the Shell is still as relevant as ever, and however you may feel about the live action movie, it does show that GitS' approach to cyberpunk doesn't feel out dated or retro even today).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T13:09:52-08:00","id":1171869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1171823#post1171823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I don't think retconning in a merger is hard to do, having them merge in the \u201cnow\u201d of the setting would be a fairly bigger deal compared to having them always been that way as initially suggested.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. And for what it's worth, the notion of having them merge in the \u201cnow\u201d never occurred to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1171823#post1171823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the big reasons is what I generally refer to the \u201cscientist vs. engineer\u201d split. The predominant mentality of the Etherites is science. That is, the rational expansion of their understanding of the universe, from which they can create functional models, from which they can do stuff. The predominant mentality of the Adepts is engineering. They take an existing model, and expand that, and themselves, and then what they can do, with it.<br /> <br /> Asking the VAs to operate in the SoE's academia and formalities would be very difficult. Asking the SoE's to operate in the VA's individualistic and anachristic social structures would likewise not work well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed on the first point (though VA culture <i>has</i> evolved over time, and I'm not so sure a modern VA would be quite as out of place in academia as his twenty-years-ago counterpart would have been); not so sure about the second. One thing about the Etherites is that their sheer variety brings in quite a bit of individualism and anarchy already \u2014 there are, for instance, the Dissidents, who are practically defined by being individualistic and anarchic. <br /> <br /> But again, I wasn't actually suggesting an in-setting merger of two well-established Traditions. Council politics would be more than enough to prevent that from happening. Case in point:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1171823#post1171823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neither group is going to react to, \u201cThe Ahl-i-Batin want back in, so make room and combine,\u201d well, and would probably both respond with, \u201cthey're religious mages, why don't they just join the Chorus. The Chorus could use some better representation in their ranks from the Arab world anyway.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div> And they wouldn't be wrong.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1171823#post1171823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also presupposes that the Virtual Adepts aren't going to evolve with the times as younger Adepts adjust their technology to what's cutting edge now instead of what was cutting edge 20 years ago. The idea that the cyberpunk genre is so firmly rooted in the 80s that a group inspired by it can't be adapted to confront the technological realities of the 21st century is kind of ridiculous as the genre has itself updated and adapted up until this day. Not every cyberpunk genre piece goes for the retro style of the late 80s and early 90s There's also plenty of genre entries that hold up today with minimal alterations (ex: Ghost in the Shell is still as relevant as ever, and however you may feel about the live action movie, it does show that GitS' approach to cyberpunk doesn't feel out dated or retro even today).</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said otherwise. In fact, the same can be said about nearly every sci-fi genre that the Etherites take their inspiration from, with the possible exception of Steampunk (which was explicitly retro from its conception). There's a reason why I referred to \u201cmany\u201d Etherites dabbling in retro-science rather than \u201call\u201d, as the Etherites very definitely have room for bleeding-edge Science too. My point isn't that cyberpunk is hopelessly dated; it's that it's not unique: cyberpunk Etherites make just as much sense as Steampunk Etherites do; and the former can be hard to distinguish from VAs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 12-30-2017, 04:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T13:10:51-08:00","id":1171870,"title":"","content":"Well put. As far as modern and post-modern style Virtual Adepts goes, I'll toss in the urban hip-hop types of Watch_Dogs, the cyber-prep types like Felicity from Arrow (or Oracle, the character she is not-name the way Oliver is not-Batman) or even Theo in Die Hard, and doomsday prepper types hiding in hidden bunkers full of high powered weapons. Plus whatever you want to classify groups like &quot;Anon-E-Mouse&quot; as, fashion wise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T15:16:55-08:00","id":1171901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1171770#post1171770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As they're presented in their Revised Tradition Book, the Sons of Ether could be merged with the VAs and hardly anyone would notice \u2014 especially now that cyberpunk (the basis of the VAs) has arguably turned out to be \u201csci-fi of the 90s\u201d, putting it in the same boat as the various retrotechs that so many Etherites dabble in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Er... no. Or if you do, why do you not merge the Shakravanti and the Akashic Brotherhood ? Both share the same culture and belief you could say (the Wheel of Dramah, etc.). Same with the Verbena and the Aided. However, they do not share the same practice. They do not place themselves at the same spot in their belief (not sure about my english there...). They do not share the same paradigm.<br /> <br /> Eutherites and VAs are close because they're all technomancers. Though they have no belief in common. They do not have the same goal, their roots are not located at the same place and they do not share the same paradigm. They do not see Ascension the same way for most of their members. VAs believe in a material world to transcend and wants to achieve this goal through technology. Etherites follow a different path, using technology to understand Reality and reach an understanding state that could lead them to Ascension. Nothing in common in that regard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8572,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","user":"NicoTheDuck","date":". 12-30-2017, 07:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T16:56:30-08:00","id":1171919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NicoTheDuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1171901#post1171901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Er... no. Or if you do, why do you not merge the Shakravanti and the Akashic Brotherhood ? Both share the same culture and belief you could say (the Wheel of Dramah, etc.). Same with the Verbena and the Aided. However, they do not share the same practice. They do not place themselves at the same spot in their belief (not sure about my english there...). They do not share the same paradigm.<br /> <br /> Eutherites and VAs are close because they're all technomancers. Though they have no belief in common. They do not have the same goal, their roots are not located at the same place and they do not share the same paradigm. They do not see Ascension the same way for most of their members. VAs believe in a material world to transcend and wants to achieve this goal through technology. Etherites follow a different path, using technology to understand Reality and reach an understanding state that could lead them to Ascension. Nothing in common in that regard.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree with your main point, but, really, the Aided would work just fine in the Verbena and probably much better. In fact, there isn't much about their effective defection to the Euthantoi that makes much sense. Persecuted by the Christians? How does that drive a bunch of druid sacrificers to ignore their friends and close neighbors who are going to be the core of the Verbena, who are also being so persecuted and seek commonality with a group whose ideologically closest sub-sets is remnant Graeco-Roman Mystery Cultists with the rest coming from ideological orientations that aren't even vaguely similar? (And no, you can't twist the concept of geasa to equivalency to the concepts of Dharma and Karma.... Just, no.) Not that the Grand Convocation didn't shove a lot of groups that don't really have much in common into a Sect (Euthanatos, Dreamspeakers and so on). But there would need to be some additional piece, like, say, the leadership of the Aided somehow pissed off Nightshade and her exiled them from the cool kids table and sent them over to the loser table in the corner with all the weird goth foreigners.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T17:59:30-08:00","id":1171925,"title":"","content":"In fact, my point isn't that folding the VAs into the SoE should be done; only that if you want to in an alternate setting, it wouldn't necessarily be a bad choice. As Ajax pointed out, a lot of the factions in Mage are more political than conceptual.<br /> <br /> And no, just because a Storyteller chooses to fold the technomancers together it doesn't mean that he's obliged to rearrange any other pieces if he doesn't want to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T18:35:27-08:00","id":1171931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1171925#post1171925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact, my point isn't that folding the VAs into the SoE should be done; only that if you want to in an alternate setting, it wouldn't necessarily be a bad choice. As Ajax pointed out, a lot of the factions in Mage are more political than conceptual.<br /> <br /> And no, just because a Storyteller chooses to fold the technomancers together it doesn't mean that he's obliged to rearrange any other pieces if he doesn't want to.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree with both Dataweaver and Heavy Arms. As written and conceptualized in structure and philosophy, the current version of the VA and Etherites would take something pretty damn significant to integrate. They're not coming at the same thing from different directions, they're going for different things at angles that aren't even in the same frame of reference. Coming up with something that currently or in the recent past would have brought them together.... that would be something BIG and, almost certainly with lots of repurcussions that would echo out into the Mage world. So, having the Etherites are they are and the Virtual Adepts as they are would be an awkward fit. <br /> <br /> However, cherry-picking the right moments in history might make things easier. The VAs of the 90's and onwards have gone their own way, but the refugees from the Union back in the late 50s might be ideologically malleable (and desperate) enough after their break with the Union and the time in the Cold to have found a way to amalgamate into the Etherite as yet another vein of alternative science. And there might be some compelling reasons why the Traditions would have pushed that. Starting with keeping all the technomancers/Union expats in one place making some sense... As for keeping the Batini around... well they weren't being treated much worse by the dominant Traditions than, say, the Dreamspeakers have been from the get go. So, instead of slipping away quietly in a fit of pique, they decided to tough it out. I mean, they were willing to put up with the Chorus when they joined up at the Grand Convocation, despite all that mess with the Crusades, the Reconquista, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T18:51:29-08:00","id":1171936,"title":"","content":"And keeping the Batini around would certainly help with the VA/Etherites merger: the Council does have something of an obsession with their \u201cSeats of the Spheres\u201d structure; so I could see them politically refusing to accept the VAs as a Tradition if the Seat of Correspondence is still occupied; but the Sons of Ether might be more willing to accept them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T18:56:11-08:00","id":1171937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1171919#post1171919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I agree with your main point, but, really, the Aided would work just fine in the Verbena and probably much better. In fact, there isn't much about their effective defection to the Euthantoi that makes much sense. Persecuted by the Christians? How does that drive a bunch of druid sacrificers to ignore their friends and close neighbors who are going to be the core of the Verbena, who are also being so persecuted and seek commonality with a group whose ideologically closest sub-sets is remnant Graeco-Roman Mystery Cultists with the rest coming from ideological orientations that aren't even vaguely similar? (And no, you can't twist the concept of geasa to equivalency to the concepts of Dharma and Karma.... Just, no.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I would guess it has something to do with the Aided being more focused (or would that be fixated? Hmm \u2026.) on issues of death, fate, destiny and the like rather than those of community, bloodlines, growth and so forth that the Verbena tend to focus on. But at the same time, I tend to view the Aided and the Twisters of Fate as two sides of the same coin, and the Great Wheel and Tree of Life not being mutually exclusive nor incompatible with each other. <br /> <br /> But then, I'm the sort of person who ended up having the Darwushim sect be members of the Ahl i Batin, Cult of Ecstasy and Akashic Brotherhood all at the same time, so YMMV.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T19:04:20-08:00","id":1171938,"title":"","content":"Also: the VAs don't necessarily want to transcend physical reality. Sure, many of them do; that's one of the things left over from their 90s cyberpunk days. But others\u2026 others seek to use (information) technology to understand reality (the Hypersphere) and reach Ascension. And the goals of the Etherites are all over the board, too: it is an entirely valid Etherite concept to be striving to transcend physical reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T19:05:32-08:00","id":1171939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NicoTheDuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1171901#post1171901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eutherites and VAs are close because they're all technomancers. Though they have no belief in common. They do not have the same goal, their roots are not located at the same place and they do not share the same paradigm. They do not see Ascension the same way for most of their members. VAs believe in a material world to transcend and wants to achieve this goal through technology. Etherites follow a different path, using technology to understand Reality and reach an understanding state that could lead them to Ascension. Nothing in common in that regard.</div> </div> </div> </div>This, incidentally, is why what happened to House Thig in the revised OoH book bugged me so. House Verditius are master craftsman and artificers who focus their magic through masterpieces and master The Art by mastering their craft(s); House Thig are modernists who look for new symbols and foci to work with classic Hermetic Art and theory - using a gun in place of a knife or sword being the simplest example. While both are in the realm of technomancy, they aren't the same thing. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T03:20:15-08:00","id":1171983,"title":"","content":"I agree with pretty much everything you said. Several comments though :<br /> <br /> - Concerning the Aided : The Verbena from Ireland often believe in gods and heroes (see Celtic mythology) while the Aided venerate their death. The former cherich the Cycle of Life whereas the other protect the Cycle of Reincarnation. Not quite the same. Another exemple of different paradigms living in a similar (even the same) culture.<br /> <br /> - Agreed with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> on the Batini matter. It is to be noted that they actually are around in the official setting and quite active during the time of Judgement, especially after the fall of Horizon. Am I mistaken ? Also<br /> <br /> - To <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12890_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12890\" data-vbnamecard=\"12890\">No One of Consequence</a> : Yeah well... Darwushim... I must admit it's quite happenstance they're part of the Batini. Well, may be not that a hazard. Aren't they at the root of the Tradition ? I think Lost Paths clarifies that point.<br /> <br /> - Conerning the House of Hermes, they regroup many different Paths but they are all linked by their practice. They're all Hermetics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T06:47:49-08:00","id":1171994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1171939#post1171939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This, incidentally, is why what happened to House Thig in the revised OoH book bugged me so. House Verditius are master craftsman and artificers who focus their magic through masterpieces and master The Art by mastering their craft(s); House Thig are modernists who look for new symbols and foci to work with classic Hermetic Art and theory - using a gun in place of a knife or sword being the simplest example. While both are in the realm of technomancy, they aren't the same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But its LITTERALLY pure politics. Two factions that have no true core setup uniting because &quot;all Technomancers are the same&quot; for purely political reasons makes SO much sense in the Order of Hermes. The House are as much about subfactional magical practices as they are political jockeying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T10:21:30-08:00","id":1172023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NicoTheDuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1171983#post1171983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with pretty much everything you said. Several comments though :<br /> <br /> - Concerning the Aided : The Verbena from Ireland often believe in gods and heroes (see Celtic mythology) while the Aided venerate their death. The former cherich the Cycle of Life whereas the other protect the Cycle of Reincarnation. Not quite the same. Another exemple of different paradigms living in a similar (even the same) culture.<br /> <br /> - Agreed with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> on the Batini matter. It is to be noted that they actually are around in the official setting and quite active during the time of Judgement, especially after the fall of Horizon. Am I mistaken ? Also<br /> <br /> - To <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12890_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12890\" data-vbnamecard=\"12890\">No One of Consequence</a> : Yeah well... Darwushim... I must admit it's quite happenstance they're part of the Batini. Well, may be not that a hazard. Aren't they at the root of the Tradition ? I think Lost Paths clarifies that point.<br /> <br /> - Conerning the House of Hermes, they regroup many different Paths but they are all linked by their practice. They're all Hermetics.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Cycle of Reincarnation is really much less of a part of Celtic mysticism than it really was insofar as we can determine, based on what legends and myths we have, based on what non-Celtic people thought about them, what 19th Century dudes in Britain who wanted to play dress up and modern iterations of paganism . It's more than a little amusing that the reason that &quot;druids&quot; get shoved into the Euthanatos is really more about the fact that D&amp;D said druids have the reincarnation spell in place of raise dead. In any case, the take on the Cycle that is attributed to the Verbena is pretty much 100% the part that is integral to the basic core fundamental beliefs that have been set as being those of the Celtic vein of the Verbena (which is one of the most central groups from way back to Nightshade herself). The Irish laud their heroes and their awesome death scenes, but if that's enough to put a group in the Euthanatos, its definitely a weird way to sort folks into Sects, since, well, EVERYONE does it and in other cultures that do it as much, if not more, that doesn't put them in Euthanatos. The role the Aided might have played is that of &quot;sacrificer&quot;, which does seem Euthanatos-like, and is represented in the Corriguinech, but. still, they are so close to the core Verbena that having them NOT be there, when, say, the Valdermen became Verbena... it has to be politics or else it's nothing. And no, the reason actually given for their part in being Euthanatos is just not going to cut it. Trying to equate geasa (and buada, their reverse) and the concepts from Indian religion and mysticism that dominate the Sect.... it's just not functional. The Verbena DO focus on Death. It's part of the Cycle. It's what's going to happen when you go after a lot of blood. Saying that the Aided are so death oriented that they just don't fit is really undermining the Verbena as described and limiting them artificially to half or less of the Cycle, tossing out 1/3 of the Maiden, Mother, Crone style trinities, etc.<br /> <br /> I do but that different groups might have split up into different Sects, and that might be interesting to explore (a la the Darwushim divide up between 3 Sects). But there would probably be a reason. And when there was the Grand Sorting Hat period at the Grand Convocation, it was all the groups being split up and sent to their respective tables. ALL of the Bjornaer moved from the Hermetic table to the Verbena table. Might a few have broken ranks and stayed? Probably. Ending up in Ex Misc almost certainly. There might even have been an iconoclast or two that said &quot;Nope! Dreamspeaker all the way!&quot; And, sure, it's possible that all the Bjornaer stayed buddies and there is a Bjornaer drinking club in some bar somewhere where everyone whose mystic mentor lineage goes back to House Bjornaer can take a seat and hoist a pint, but that's almost an entirely different matter. It's more in the nature of Allies, Contacts, possibly even a Chantry or even a Cabal of sorts, more than a matter of Sect. (Though, really, doesn't that seem like a great idea for a game? The Heirs of Bjornaer/Darwushim/Valderman/whatever as a cabal with members from all the Traditions that partook of the original group's mysticism?)<br /> <br /> However, there is NO link by Practice within any Sect at this point, not the Hermetics, not anyone. As per M20 p. 159, Hermetics as a group demand Alchemy, Dominion and High Ritual (but no mage is required to have all of them, so, probably at least one, but probably more? Thanks M20 for the lack of guidance on this...), but venture out to.... whew.... Chaos Magick, Art of Desire, Hypertech, Craftwork, Weird Science, Yoga, and Malficia. So there is nothing determinative about the Hermetics practice(s) that sets them apart as a group from anyone else. At all. Any mage could have any of the above or any combination of the above and NOT be a Hermetic at all or even have magic that &quot;looks Hermetic&quot; for whatever that means. The idea that Sects have some kind of magical praxis that unites them and differentiates them from the praxis of different Sects is not a part of M20 at all. It's a remnant idea from earlier editions where the ideas that are now identified as Focus were handled differently. In essence, by not having a category of magical praxis that ties together the magic of members of a Sect, sort of an uber-Focus, M20 has de facto come down and set things up so that Sects are almost entirely political and social, not technical/practical/mystical groupings.(Which is something lost in the game IMO) I mean, COULD you have a Hermetic who uses Voodoo? Sure. Could you have a VA who uses Voodoo? Absolutely. They could probably be differentiated by their Instruments, but, just as likely, they could not be. So what makes one dude a Hermetic and another a VA? It's who they hang with. Not so much in who their friends, but more in the sense of which professional association they have a membership in and what union meetings they attend. Being a Hermetic doesn't unit them in any other way, anymore. <br /> <br /> Which pulls us back to the OP. There is really nothing at all that, as a matter of how their magic is done, that keeps VAs from being Etherites. Even politically, as Dataweaver points out, the Etherites are very ecumenical in what the goal of all THIS is, so it would be very easy, ideologically, to fold them in. But, as a matter of ideology, it would be a lot harder to embrace all the goals of the Etherites under the umbrella of the set of Ascension-type goals prevalent in the VAs. What makes the two different? Really, it's the social ramifications of their history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 12-31-2017, 01:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T11:12:24-08:00","id":1172031,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't go quite that far: even in M20, I can't imagine an atheist Chorister or an ItXer who practices witchcraft. But yeah; M20 blurred the lines a <i>lot</i>, and for the most part there is no specific Paradigm, Practice, or Instrument that you <i>must</i> have to join any particular group. (Going by memory, exceptions include the Verbena, for whom Witchcraft is singled out as a Practice common to all Verbenae.) That said: while the individual parts of the Focus can all vary, there's still an implication that there's a core principle that informs the choices of those parts: you might have an Etherite who Practices Witchcraft; but even so he'll have a Science-compatible Paradigm, making him a rational mystic. <br /> <br /> Still, I agree with your core point: M20 factions are a lot more political and/or social in nature in M20 than they were in earlier editions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T11:55:59-08:00","id":1172036,"title":"","content":"How has M20 actually changed anything here?<br /> <br /> The Traditions have always been highly socio-political groups, whether a given one clusters around a style of magic or not. The Traditions have never actually strenuously demanded specific Paradigms, Practices, and Instruments as M20 defines them. M20's Focus creation system doesn't say - anywhere - that the Traditions no longer have internal cultural norms that members are expected to abide by.<br /> <br /> Not having lists of required and banned Focus elements for each Tradition/etc. isn't a message that any and all combinations of them work in every Tradition. It's just that the game expects us to use our brains and make sure it makes sense. The Yoga Practice makes perfect sense for members of House Tytalus to use, even if what they do wouldn't be seen as yoga in common parlance, if you look at what the Yoga Practice actually means. <br /> <br /> Sure we don't have M20 versions of the Traditionbook levels of detail on each Traditions philosophies and styles, but M20 has more about each by just recommending Focus elements for splats than any previous corebook really managed.<br /> <br /> They idea that anything has radically changed in M20 around this baffles me.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T17:24:03-08:00","id":1172116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NicoTheDuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1171983#post1171983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- To <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12890_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12890\" data-vbnamecard=\"12890\">No One of Consequence</a> : Yeah well... Darwushim... I must admit it's quite happenstance they're part of the Batini. Well, may be not that a hazard. Aren't they at the root of the Tradition ? I think Lost Paths clarifies that point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, in my case, I'm just the sort of person that, after Time of Judgment, when I went back and adjusted (or in some cases outright rebuilt) the entire setting for my own tastes and needs (games I run tend to be slightly different than what some people are used to), when I wrote up all of the factions for each Tradition and Craft, I had more than a few who were clearly either the same group or came from the same group but were members of more than one Tradition. So, under the list of sub factions in the Akashic Brotherhood's Jnani, the Cult of Ecstasy's Seekers of the Divine, and as one of the Ahl i Batin's main factions, you have the Darwushim, all written up almost identically save for slight wording variations to stress which part of seeing past material illusions to touch the face of Allah and become one with his Unity that Tradition is more focused on. Likewise the Hermetic House Bjournaer and the Verbena Twisters of Fate faction that the House's founders came from in the first place, or the three different groups from the Hermetics, Euthanatoi and Celestial Chorus who all descend from the Ixoi. One of the reasons I can do this - besides the obvious that I'm the ST - is that I managed to simplify each Tradition's overarching philosophy into a core idea and have their factions approach it from slightly different angles, (and a part of this is why each Tradition has which primary Sphere that everyone learns the first level of as part of their initiation) and sometimes a smaller pre-Grand Convocation faction finds they can express themselves in more than one way. I suspect this is made even easier for me by the fact that I've never looked at any M20 material and when people mention things like Paradigms and Practices as being something apparently now a game mechanic instead of roleplaying aids (yes? no?), I only have some contextual idea of what they're talking about. This is not to say that M20 is wrong or anything, just that what I tend to do with Mage diverged from whatever OP decided to do, so sometimes my takes on things are different. As always, YMMV.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T18:42:30-08:00","id":1172124,"title":"","content":"Ok... I've got pretty confused with your ideas. My mind is clearer now.<br /> <br /> The Verbenae and Aided are different. They all believe in the Cycle of Life but the Verbenae do not place themselves as judges of this Cycle while the Aided do. As do the Euthanatoi, they think they are the keepers of the Wheel (I agree, meta-speaking, that the Aided are an invention to get Death priests among the Celtic poeple, however, let's consider them as part of the WoD as they are). This major difference between these factions explain why during the Grand Convocation the Aided (as few as they probably were) chose to join the Chakravanti instead of the Verbenae (may be these ones could not accept them or even chased them !)<br /> <br /> The same is true with the Dervish (though this faction actually exist in our world). They could not be part of the Cult of Ecstasy because even if they practice magick through their trance, their belief is centered on the almighty power of Allah. This is not compatible with the Cultist belief.<br /> <br /> Those kind of diferences caused the Himalyan war between the Euthanatoi and the Akashic Brotherhood.<br /> <br /> And I disagree. M20 did not blur things. In my opinion, it clarified much. The first editions of Mage were misunderstood even by the authors from my point of view. They matured the matter and came back a few years later with this edition which is closer to the post-modernism philosophy upon which the game was created in the first place. People can share a belief and interpret this belief in many ways and transfer these different understanding in differents practices. Yes, Traditions are often political groups. But they still gather poeple with close beliefs and interpretations. That is why you can have same labeled-practices in different paradigms and Traditions. Well at least, that's what I think.<br /> <br /> Happy new year to all !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T20:42:53-08:00","id":1172156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NicoTheDuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1172124#post1172124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok... I've got pretty confused with your ideas. My mind is clearer now.<br /> <br /> The Verbenae and Aided are different. They all believe in the Cycle of Life but the Verbenae do not place themselves as judges of this Cycle while the Aided do. As do the Euthanatoi, they think they are the keepers of the Wheel (I agree, meta-speaking, that the Aided are an invention to get Death priests among the Celtic poeple, however, let's consider them as part of the WoD as they are). This major difference between these factions explain why during the Grand Convocation the Aided (as few as they probably were) chose to join the Chakravanti instead of the Verbenae (may be these ones could not accept them or even chased them !)<br /> <br /> The same is true with the Dervish (though this faction actually exist in our world). They could not be part of the Cult of Ecstasy because even if they practice magick through their trance, their belief is centered on the almighty power of Allah. This is not compatible with the Cultist belief.<br /> mys<br /> Those kind of diferences caused the Himalyan war between the Euthanatoi and the Akashic Brotherhood.<br /> <br /> And I disagree. M20 did not blur things. In my opinion, it clarified much. The first editions of Mage were misunderstood even by the authors from my point of view. They matured the matter and came back a few years later with this edition which is closer to the post-modernism philosophy upon which the game was created in the first place. People can share a belief and interpret this belief in many ways and transfer these different understanding in differents practices. Yes, Traditions are often political groups. But they still gather poeple with close beliefs and interpretations. That is why you can have same labeled-practices in different paradigms and Traditions. Well at least, that's what I think.<br /> <br /> Happy new year to all !</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's where we're going to part ways. I don't accept the Aided as part of the WoD as is BECAUSE they are just an attempt to shoehorn in a Celtic Euthanatos and there is nothing about it that makes sense other than just that. I would buy it with a SIMPLE fix. A bit of fluff that talks about why the 100% core Verbena Aided aren't welcome in the Verbena. I mean, the VALDERMEN, who are much more Euthanatos-like and the Bjornaer who have been in bed with the intolerant Diedne-killing Hermetics are WARMLY welcomed into the Verbena. But as is. NOPE. There is nothing to the idea that the Verbena aren't judgmental about death. Verbena are all about judging people. All about punishing people violating their perception of the natural order. I really don't even question putting groups with fuck-all to do with each other together, especially when the groups are non-European. I mean, the Euthanatos tossed the Madzimbabwe and the Chakravanti and the Greek Mystery Cults all together (and what did THEY do to piss off the Verbena... .I mean, does any mythopoetic mysticism get more Verbena than the Story of Demeter and Persephone?). It's just the way the Aided aren't teased out, some non-difference is set up as a different based on a complete lack of understanding of what geasa are and how they worked. Give me a REASON that makes sense. It doesn't have to be magical, because magic doesn't matter so much, Sects are political groups. <br /> <br /> There are Jewish Dervishes. So it's more than just Allah. And Timothy Leary's bible actually makes sense when read in the sense of some Sufi Mysticism. <br /> <br /> I didn't say it blurred things. I just said that when things are said like &quot;This Tradition has this practice&quot; for whatever value you want to give that word (as Focus, as Practice, as common Instruments, as some sort of &quot;ideological twine that holds all these folks together&quot;), it's not longer a statement with any material validity. Focus has taken the concept of Traditions having some kind of proprietary mojo and largely deep six-ed it. There are some probably commonalities that might occur betwee most members, but nothing that's necessary. Traditions are now just political groups. There is nothing that mystically binds together the magical praxis of the members of Tradition or Sect or, in reverse, anything that decisively sets them apart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T20:51:32-08:00","id":1172158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1172031#post1172031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't go quite that far: even in M20, I can't imagine an atheist Chorister or an ItXer who practices witchcraft. But yeah; M20 blurred the lines a <i>lot</i>, and for the most part there is no specific Paradigm, Practice, or Instrument that you <i>must</i> have to join any particular group. (Going by memory, exceptions include the Verbena, for whom Witchcraft is singled out as a Practice common to all Verbenae.) That said: while the individual parts of the Focus can all vary, there's still an implication that there's a core principle that informs the choices of those parts: you might have an Etherite who Practices Witchcraft; but even so he'll have a Science-compatible Paradigm, making him a rational mystic.<br /> <br /> Still, I agree with your core point: M20 factions are a lot more political and/or social in nature in M20 than they were in earlier editions.</div> </div> </div> </div>My feelings are this are informed by going to look at the mages in the Book of Secrets examples of developed Foci. Read those and and come back and say that they haven't taken those pools of color that were the ideas of Practice and social identity as a Sect and just gone finger-paintining with them. If THOSE are typical mages, then a Sect is just a political affiliation. If that. <br /> <br /> I've seen Brucato say that he feels the game should really be about Orphans and very individualized perceptions of magic and that all the politics of the setting really got in the way of the core concepts of the game. And I would say that M20, in its bones, bears that out. Honestly, it's an interesting way to look at it and I think we're going to dig into that and see how it plays out in the next Mage chronicle. BUT, and this is a big but, it does undermine some of the pillars that hold up the setting of the game as is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T22:54:23-08:00","id":1172194,"title":"","content":"As a note, there are Valdaermen that ended up in the Euthanatos: they're just in the Norse themed Keepers of Yggdrasil (because the Valdaermen aren't Celts), not the Aided. And the non-mystic reason? The Aided were pissed off at the Old Faith for joining forces with the predominately Christian Order of Hermes and Messianic Singers, and splintered off only to be drawn back into the Traditions later by the rest of the European proto-Euthanatoi (like some of the Valdaermen) more comfortably aligned politically with people that weren't cool with Christianity being forced on people.<br /> <br /> As to the whole, &quot;There is nothing that mystically binds together the magical praxis of the members of Tradition or Sect or, in reverse, anything that decisively sets them apart.&quot; thing?<br /> <br /> Can I get any argument that this is actually new? The Focus system in M20, to me, didn't change anything. It clarified what was already there. By Revised, every Tradition had technomancer styled factions. Every Tradition had been expanded a lot from their 1e archetypal imaginings. The whole line of thinking about something being different about M20 fails, because it seems to want to claim what was already there wasn't.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T06:41:38-08:00","id":1172242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1172156#post1172156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's where we're going to part ways. I don't accept the Aided as part of the WoD as is BECAUSE they are just an attempt to shoehorn in a Celtic Euthanatos and there is nothing about it that makes sense other than just that. I would buy it with a SIMPLE fix. A bit of fluff that talks about why the 100% core Verbena Aided aren't welcome in the Verbena. I mean, the VALDERMEN, who are much more Euthanatos-like and the Bjornaer who have been in bed with the intolerant Diedne-killing Hermetics are WARMLY welcomed into the Verbena.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, we disagree. The Verbenae judge, though they do not decide for the sake of the Wheel who has to live and who has top die. They react to events and are sometimes (often ?) vengeful mages, but they do not decide in the name of Destiny and Karma (or their Celtic version). The fluff is there I think. The Aided are not welcomed by the Verbena because of their practice considered as a consequence of great Hubris and misunderstanding of the Cycle of Life. Again, their struggle is close to the one opposing the Akashic Brotherhood and the Euthanatos. They share the same culture, religion or belief but do not interpret their role in the world the same way. Well... in the end, let's get the correct scaling here. How many are the Aided ? 60 poeple ? ^^ Not really a reason to fight for it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Concerning the Bjornaer, their practice is a Hermetic one. That's not because it's close to Nature that it's Verbena. It oversimplifies the whole matter in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T09:50:24-08:00","id":1172291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NicoTheDuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1172124#post1172124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The same is true with the Dervish (though this faction actually exist in our world). They could not be part of the Cult of Ecstasy because even if they practice magick through their trance, their belief is centered on the almighty power of Allah. This is not compatible with the Cultist belief.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would it be incompatible? The practice of Sama is aimed at reaching wadj (a trance like ecstatic state) and/or khamra (&quot;spiritual drunkenness&quot;) with the end goal of unveiling divine mysteries and gaining spiritual knowledge. There are a number of Ecstatic sects who seek to touch the power of the Divine, and the story of how Rumi came up with Sama in the first place - hearing the chant of &quot;there is no god but Allah&quot; in the hammering of the goldsmiths while walking through the market, suddenly thrusting him into a state of wadj and compelled to spin - bears an uncanny resemblance to being made aware of the Lakashim for the first time. <br /> <br /> As for the Aided, I think Malcolm Shepherd (or it may have been Jess Heinig, I can't recall at this point) once told me that his read on them was that they were something of a bunch of elitist snobs who joined the Euthanatos primarily because all of their omens and readings said they'd die out if they didn't. I may be misremembering though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T14:53:32-08:00","id":1172391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1172158#post1172158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My feelings are this are informed by going to look at the mages in the Book of Secrets examples of developed Foci. Read those and and come back and say that they haven't taken those pools of color that were the ideas of Practice and social identity as a Sect and just gone finger-paintining with them. If THOSE are typical mages, then a Sect is just a political affiliation. If that.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm not seeing the issue here. Are you under the impression that these guys are Orphans unless otherwise specified? They might be; but even if they are, I don't see how that makes the Traditions nothing more than socio-political structures. If I had to guess which Tradition Able Ferox is a member of, my first guess would be the Virtual Adepts. Ashpaw Ten Sticks would be a natural fit for the Dreamspeakers; Corvia Delbaeth looks very much like a Verbena; Dr. Hans von Roth <i>is</i> an Etherite; Sanjay Sachdeva is an agent of Iteration X; and while Tanisha Royale isn't in the Akashayana, it's easily the Tradition that she's most compatible with.<br /> <br /> Conversely, the idea that Able might be in the Order of Hermes seems highly unlikely. Ashpaw probably isn't a Chorister. Corvia doesn't strike me as Euthanatos material. And Tanisha isn't going to be joining the Sisterhood of Hypollyta any time soon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1172158#post1172158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've seen Brucato say that he feels the game should really be about Orphans and very individualized perceptions of magic and that all the politics of the setting really got in the way of the core concepts of the game. And I would say that M20, in its bones, bears that out. Honestly, it's an interesting way to look at it and I think we're going to dig into that and see how it plays out in the next Mage chronicle. BUT, and this is a big but, it does undermine some of the pillars that hold up the setting of the game as is.</div> </div> </div> </div> Brucato certainly is on record as wanting to destigmatize the Orphans. But again, I don't see how that removes Focus from the Traditions. Each group in M20 has a section on Focus which presents the gist of how mages in that group work their magick; and you're not going to be a member of that group if your Focus isn't compatible with its Focus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T17:57:08-08:00","id":1172462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1172194#post1172194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As to the whole, \u201cThere is nothing that mystically binds together the magical praxis of the members of Tradition or Sect or, in reverse, anything that decisively sets them apart\u201d thing?<br /> <br /> Can I get any argument that this is actually new? <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I actually would argue that this is something of a new take to be honest.<br /> <br /> I read a few of your post and while I generally agree with you, especially about the rise of technomancer factions within the Traditions, I feel that the Revised Edition core book and many others actually promote strongly the idea that the Traditions are cohesive groups because they have both mystical beliefs and practices which differ from one another and that that is the primary reason for the division between their respective groups.<br /> <br /> I really feel that many of the revised edition books were written from this prespective and that, in fact, M20 HAS gone in a new direction.<br /> <br /> Chapter one of the Revised Edition Storyteller\u2019s Handbook is a prime example of this, it is decisively states in numerous passages that what divides the Traditions is their different theories and practices regarding magic and that without those differences there would not be Traditions at all.<br /> <br /> Now, I\u2019m not agreeing with this perspective, but I am acknowledging that it comes up rather frequently in many of the Revised Edition books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T18:58:50-08:00","id":1172477,"title":"","content":"The problem is when Revised is using &quot;practice&quot; in that sense, it isn't what M20 uses as a Practice as part of a Focus.<br /> <br /> For example, all of the Chorus might use religious devotion as a common small p practice (which is very clearly the case in Revised). However in both Revised and M20, this can still express itself in another of ways. Revised puts it all into foci, but M20 standardizes things like Practices as well. A Chorister that uses guided meditation on the unity of the One is using very different Practice and Instrument combos from a Chorister that leads people in elaborate Catholic mass inspired services. Revised considers this all the same &quot;practice,&quot; and M20's Practices doesn't create something new.<br /> <br /> It feels to me too much like an equivocation over terminology than a real demonstrate of a change in how things work in each edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-03T09:47:53-08:00","id":1173019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1172391#post1172391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm not seeing the issue here. Are you under the impression that these guys are Orphans unless otherwise specified? They might be; but even if they are, I don't see how that makes the Traditions nothing more than socio-political structures. If I had to guess which Tradition Able Ferox is a member of, my first guess would be the Virtual Adepts. Ashpaw Ten Sticks would be a natural fit for the Dreamspeakers; Corvia Delbaeth looks very much like a Verbena; Dr. Hans von Roth <i>is</i> an Etherite; Sanjay Sachdeva is an agent of Iteration X; and while Tanisha Royale isn't in the Akashayana, it's easily the Tradition that she's most compatible with.<br /> <br /> Conversely, the idea that Able might be in the Order of Hermes seems highly unlikely. Ashpaw probably isn't a Chorister. Corvia doesn't strike me as Euthanatos material. And Tanisha isn't going to be joining the Sisterhood of Hypollyta any time soon.<br /> <br /> Brucato certainly is on record as wanting to destigmatize the Orphans. But again, I don't see how that removes Focus from the Traditions. Each group in M20 has a section on Focus which presents the gist of how mages in that group work their magick; and you're not going to be a member of that group if your Focus isn't compatible with its Focus.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that these are characeters that are supposed to show how the Focus system works and that you are having to make guesses about what Tradition they belong to pretty much locks down my point. If Focus and Sect ere related in anything other than the most tenuous way, then mentioning what Sect such a character belonged to would be front and center, including if they are (or even were) an Orphan. The fact that their Sect is so utterly irrelevant it is actually NEVER mentioned in describing their methodology and philosophy and practice of magic is a decisive indicator of what I've been pointing out. If your Sect actually MATTERED to how you do magic, it would be there. It isn't And really, the exceptions are just that, exceptions which come close to proving the rule. The Sects are political units created from a shared history. They aren't really anything more than broadly relevant to magic and, if they are to any degree, it's not a requirement, adhereing to a particular Sect way of doing things comes across as somewhat quaint, old-fashioned and shows something of a lack of creativity. <br /> <br /> As someone who loves the old Foundation/Pillar system so much you want to keep it current for some outlier mages and who has worked so hard to create a new take on magic for the Union, it seems like the way BoS and, to a degree, M20, handles how Focus relates to Sect would go against your grain. It' effectively unfettering mages from really anything other than a personal way of doing magic that may sorta look like what those other people over here I sometimes hang out with when I'm not with you guys in my cabal, but, really, isn't in any meaningful way. <br /> <br /> Admittedly, you CAN say that those initial Practice suggestions under the Sect descriptions aren't really so much suggestions as fundamentals that, to really get any benefit from Sect membership, you have to, if not master, at least get a journeyman's knowledge of. It's probably not to much to say that all Verbena have Witchcraft as a core to their Practice then add on infuences from other Practices or synthesize them in for an individual mage's &quot;take&quot; on their personal way of casting. Or that Hermetics have High Ritual Magic (and probably Alchemy? I'm not so sure Dominance should be required...), Etherites have Weird Science and so on. (Yeah, that does leave some folks in an odd place, particularly when the Sect in question is really something of a political alliance without much in the way of commonality of practice, like, say, the Euthanatos).<br /> <br /> But that is NOT the way the game, as it is currently being presented, is going. Brucato isn't trying to destigmatize Orphans. I mean, in the context of the game world, he really hasn't besides a small leg up by having them be the Ex Misc of the New Traditions... I mean, Disparate Alliance. That's not much. The Union still wants to forcibly recruit them and the Traditions are just a step behind most of the time or, institutionally, looks down on them. What he has explicitly stated (mostly on Facebook), is that he really feels that, to him, the core of Mage should be about the development of individualized magic to the exclusion of any kind of groupthink and, further, to not even having the Factions or Sects at all. That isn't destigmatizing them as much as putting them front and center and pushing everything else to the sides. It's the exact opposite of DA's Foundation/Pillar system. It's a World of Orphans, each of them experiencing an individualized progression on a personal quest to understand the way they, and they alone, experience altering reality through the power of their wills. And his Focus system (which BTW, I do really like) has enacted his ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-03T11:42:32-08:00","id":1173053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1173019#post1173019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that is NOT the way the game, as it is currently being presented, is going. Brucato isn't trying to destigmatize Orphans. I mean, in the context of the game world, he really hasn't besides a small leg up by having them be the Ex Misc of the New Traditions... I mean, Disparate Alliance. That's not much. The Union still wants to forcibly recruit them and the Traditions are just a step behind most of the time or, institutionally, looks down on them. What he has explicitly stated (mostly on Facebook), is that he really feels that, to him, the core of Mage should be about the development of individualized magic to the exclusion of any kind of groupthink and, further, to not even having the Factions or Sects at all. That isn't destigmatizing them as much as putting them front and center and pushing everything else to the sides. It's the exact opposite of DA's Foundation/Pillar system. It's a World of Orphans, each of them experiencing an individualized progression on a personal quest to understand the way they, and they alone, experience altering reality through the power of their wills. And his Focus system (which BTW, I do really like) has enacted his ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is not true. All Traditions have their prefered practices and there are minor groups using minor practices in all Traditions. In a way, your statements are both true and false. I think you forget a major factor here: the education one. Poeple grow up in different sub-cultures all other the world. The Traditions are not all political, they are obviously cultural too. The Witchcraft practiced by the Celtic witches is not the same that the Witchcract practiced by African sorcerers and marabouts. And it is different from the practice of the Shamans from North America or Russia (which has its own version of shamanism) and it is different from the animism of the Taoists. All these Traditions share bits of practice and beliefs in various forms. They are similar in some ways and different in others. A world of Orphans would not be in the game's spirit where Magick is learnt with apprenticeship. Mages learn their magick from masters and mentors from a particular sub-culture and will (with often minor changes) practice Magick the same way. And Mages share. They do because they're lost if they do not.<br /> <br /> In Mage: The Ascension, Magick is dangerous Because of Paradox. A world of Orphans would lead to few Mages accomplishing anything relevant, or even anything at all. At the begining of the Traditions, they gathered to Horizon because of that. They were dying at the hand of the Order of Reason, but that's not the only reason. They were dying because Magick was dying. Paradox appeared and few could handled it. They formed the Traditions to survive. Even if it meant allying with groups from pretty different cultures, especially if yours has few members.<br /> <br /> The cultural aspect of the game is at its core. It's so important that everything is the about the culture dominion of one group over all, hence the Ascension War.<br /> <br /> I must have misunderstood your point somewhere. If so, do not hesitate to correct me. English is not my native langage and I can sometimes lose meaning in the translations ^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-03T12:32:54-08:00","id":1173063,"title":"","content":"His point was that the game's developer, Phil Brucato, <i>wants</i> it to be \u201ca world of Orphans\u201d, and is doing what he can to push the game in that direction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-03T12:57:31-08:00","id":1173066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1173063#post1173063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">His point was that the game's developer, Phil Brucato, <i>wants</i> it to be \u201ca world of Orphans\u201d, and is doing what he can to push the game in that direction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah ok. Then I have not that impression. It seems to me that the game is more understood now than twe decades ago, even by the author. What he had at the begining was a &quot;what could be&quot; world of Mage in the sense that he wanted the game to be multicultural but lacked the knowledge or the understanding to make it so (but I might be mistaken...). The understanding of sub-cultures and their practice is much more realistic now that the practices are not considered limited to the Traditions. There <i>are</i> several types of witchcraft, alchemy, shamanism, etc. It should not be restricted to one Tradtion or the other. However, the cultural background of each Tradition is much more relevant now that beliefs, practices and instruments are separated. This trinity seems more realistic to me since cultural habits often inherits from this logic: what do you believe in ? How does it affect your life ? With what do you act upon it ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T10:21:23-08:00","id":1173253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NicoTheDuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1173066#post1173066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah ok. Then I have not that impression. It seems to me that the game is more understood now than twe decades ago, even by the author. What he had at the begining was a &quot;what could be&quot; world of Mage in the sense that he wanted the game to be multicultural but lacked the knowledge or the understanding to make it so (but I might be mistaken...). The understanding of sub-cultures and their practice is much more realistic now that the practices are not considered limited to the Traditions. There <i>are</i> several types of witchcraft, alchemy, shamanism, etc. It should not be restricted to one Tradtion or the other. However, the cultural background of each Tradition is much more relevant now that beliefs, practices and instruments are separated. This trinity seems more realistic to me since cultural habits often inherits from this logic: what do you believe in ? How does it affect your life ? With what do you act upon it ?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How are they separated exactly? I don't see any evidence of any of this except for the ligthest of glosses. There are those bits in the Sect descriptions about the Foci of the members, but they are are barely even suggestions, as they go from one or so &quot;main ideas&quot; to exploding outwards into appreciably more than half the list of possible Practices. What I'm looking for is something in, say, the section on Focus where it explicitly goes into how SECT not the mage's personal beliefs, but those aspects of those beliefs that are shared with the member of their Sect in such a way that they create a meaningful distinction by which that shared belief distinguishes them from the shared personal beliefs of members of other Sects. <br /> <br /> This seems particularly pertinent with, say, some of the Disparates (Kopa Loei, Wu Lung, Taftani, etc.), who are supposed to be non-joiners, not just for political reasons (e.g. not wanting to bow before the Big Three), but because they had a very firm collective idea of how magic worked and didn't want the Traditions' paws all over their belief system. <br /> <br /> In fact, I don't see the relevance you are describing at all. In pretty much every place, eccumenicism is the rule, rather than the exception. Which is fine. That's not actually a weakness of the Traditions. The Chorus would be less interesting if it was hardcore fundamental Christians who reject all other notions of divinity, or the Hermetics were particularized into static Houses without the &quot;creative playground&quot; of Ex Misc. and the willingness to, on occasion, pull the European High Magical stick out of their buts and recognize common ground with other similar ritualized practices like the Wu Lung in Hong Lei and the Ngoma in Ngoma...<br /> <br /> I am less interested in the &quot;purity of belief&quot; with regard to a specific culture's folkways (except where that's relevant, see above for Disparates) than I am in seeing some actual hard crunchy-style evidence of SECT culture that represents a group-think about the way in which that particular sect does magic that both binds it together and differentiates it from other sects. Though that is implied to some degree, it is an implication that doesn't really manifest currently, and, in fact, the weight of current trends is in the opposing direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T10:48:09-08:00","id":1173261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NicoTheDuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1172242#post1172242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indeed, we disagree. The Verbenae judge, though they do not decide for the sake of the Wheel who has to live and who has top die. They react to events and are sometimes (often ?) vengeful mages, but they do not decide in the name of Destiny and Karma (or their Celtic version). The fluff is there I think. The Aided are not welcomed by the Verbena because of their practice considered as a consequence of great Hubris and misunderstanding of the Cycle of Life. Again, their struggle is close to the one opposing the Akashic Brotherhood and the Euthanatos. They share the same culture, religion or belief but do not interpret their role in the world the same way. Well... in the end, let's get the correct scaling here. How many are the Aided ? 60 poeple ? ^^ Not really a reason to fight for it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Concerning the Bjornaer, their practice is a Hermetic one. That's not because it's close to Nature that it's Verbena. It oversimplifies the whole matter in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Celts do the Verbenae thing. Not the Karma thing. There isn't any more of an easy translation of that concept into what we know of druidic mysticism than there is into modern Western ideas. It is NOT equivalent to geasa. That is a not really an oversimplification, it's a complete misunderstanding of what geasa are and how they worked. So, by practice, they should be back in the Verbena, not withstanding any mental gymnastics to the contrary. Transmigration of souls found in Irish myths and legends isn't even close to being like the cycle of reincarnation. It's just not. <br /> <br /> HOWEVER, what I keep saying that gets lost here is that I am actually somewhat okay with having the Aided in the Euthanatos. Mostly because, even though the Wheel of Karma/Dharma is really hardcore Chakravanti mysticism, the Euthanatos aren't the Chakravanti and never have been. In fact, the Chakravanti are effectively the largest group in a plurality of groups that don't share anything specific as a whole (or didn't originally). There is something of a loose continuum of beliefs that overlap from one group to another that doesn't/didn't really join together in and of themselves. It was more of an &quot;othering&quot; external to the groups that were shoved together by people who didn't understand them and didn't even want to try to understand them. The Madzimbabwe aren't about reincarnation. The Mystery Cults aren't really either as it's about continuance of the individual in way in that would be anathema to dharma, the kind of thing that leads to demons and ghosts and having karma pull a soul down.<br /> <br /> So, since the Euthanatos DON'T (didn't) really have a coherent core ideology, why not have a renegade bunch of Celts who are for all intents and purposes perfectly good Verbena join up? The Bjornaer were almost perfectly good Hermetics for several centuries (from the old Ars Magica stuff, it does seem like Bjornaer was a reluctant joinee, but, hey, if Diedne is doing it, right?), but the Verbena were cool with them joining up. I just want a STORY to it. Why did these particular Verbena leave and throw in with the group that was mistakenly being grouped together as &quot;icky death mages&quot;? <br /> <br /> Moreover, I am also very cool with, having such a story in hand, having the Aided and the other groups in the Euthanatos actually bend towards each other as they establish a coherent group identity after having been together for so long. I mean, there would have been a lot of exposure to each other's ideas and they would start to notice that each group had some ways of handling situation that just worked better than the way their traditional praxis handled it. (Like, say, the Chakravanti noticing that the Madzimbabwe had some mad ghost handling skills that might make their attempts to deal with lost souls that need to find their way back to the Wheel better than what they had been doing and so on). In the end, after half a millennium, though there are sub-groups that are still identifiable as being the ideological descendants of the Chakravanti who call themselves Chakravanti, they would, unlike the original Chakravanti, share some pool of mystical knowhow created from the collaboration of all the constituent groups of the Euthanatos over time. <br /> <br /> In which case, the modern Aided, who would probably still be Verbena enough to join back up on an individual or group basis if that was in the cards, would partake of that pool and would be able to use some ideas in their Practices that would be more African or Indian or Greek or Voodoo with a Celtic gloss. <br /> <br /> But I still want that story about why they chose to or were forced to join the weirdo/goth kids table in the Convocation cafeteria instead of sitting at the popular kids table with Nightshade and her cronies....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T11:28:15-08:00","id":1173266,"title":"","content":"Just throwing this out there\u2026 The Batini cannot have Entropy. It's not \u201cEntropy is rare in their ranks\u201d the way Dimensional Science is rare in Iteration X's ranks; it's a flat-out prohibition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T11:37:43-08:00","id":1173269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1173253#post1173253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How are they separated exactly? I don't see any evidence of any of this except for the ligthest of glosses. There are those bits in the Sect descriptions about the Foci of the members, but they are are barely even suggestions, as they go from one or so &quot;main ideas&quot; to exploding outwards into appreciably more than half the list of possible Practices.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course they're suggestions. Why would you want it to be otherwise ? Belonging to the same group does not mean every Mage of the group is the same. Mages from a given group share belief, not practice. It is obvious that poeple gather for political reasons, but it is not enough to bring together an entire Tradition. Belief is necessary too. On paper, it should come first (and hopefully, that's the other way around ! For the sake of plot, intrigue ^^)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1173253#post1173253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I'm looking for is something in, say, the section on Focus where it explicitly goes into how SECT not the mage's personal beliefs, but those aspects of those beliefs that are shared with the member of their Sect in such a way that they create a meaningful distinction by which that shared belief distinguishes them from the shared personal beliefs of members of other Sects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, why would you want anything at all to be so rigid ? It serves absolutely no purpose, and anyway, this is not realistic. I already gave examples of different practices being cross-traditions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1173253#post1173253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This seems particularly pertinent with, say, some of the Disparates (Kopa Loei, Wu Lung, Taftani, etc.), who are supposed to be non-joiners, not just for political reasons (e.g. not wanting to bow before the Big Three), but because they had a very firm collective idea of how magic worked and didn't want the Traditions' paws all over their belief system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that's true. Separately.<br /> They share nothing in common. Bata'a share nothing with the Hollow Ones or the Batini for example. And well, the Disparate Alliance, is pretty much only political. But well, this should be left to personal interpretation and is another matter I think.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1173253#post1173253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact, I don't see the relevance you are describing at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I know.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1173253#post1173253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am less interested in the &quot;purity of belief&quot; with regard to a specific culture's folkways (except where that's relevant, see above for Disparates) than I am in seeing some actual hard crunchy-style evidence of SECT culture that represents a group-think about the way in which that particular sect does magic that both binds it together and differentiates it from other sects. Though that is implied to some degree, it is an implication that doesn't really manifest currently, and, in fact, the weight of current trends is in the opposing direction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where I think you are mistaken is that you seem to think that under the Witchcraft section, there can only be one sort of Witchcraft and that it should be associated to a given Sect. Same with the other practices. But this is not the case and shoult not be. Each type of a particular practice is associated to a particular belief. The spells a celtic witch usually cast would not use the same tools or words that a spanish brujah will use. To give another examples of known Mages, both Morgane la F\u00e9e and Harry Potter use Witchcraft though they are not from the same Tradition and share not belief in common. A given practice is not limited to a given Sect. It is simply not.<br /> <br /> The practices described in the core-book are examples of practices that the Mage can follow. This list is not exhaustive. You can see it another way. Take a Verbena witch casting a spell with magick words. In which langage would she speak ? There are plenty of answers to that question ! And the correct answer for a given Mage is linked to her particular belief (because this is the core of Mage):<br /> - She could speak the langage of the Devil if she has a Christian background and follow, say, a Satanist cult (which has not always been pejorative),<br /> - She could speak the anciant words of the Thatha D\u00e9 Danann if she believes in celtic mythology.<br /> etc.<br /> Everything is about fluff. I'll admit that. But it makes the character more realistic to detail those kind of things.<br /> <br /> And guess what ? Same is true with belief. A specific belief does not involve a specific practice and is not associated to a specific Sect. An Hermetic Mage could be an Alchemist or a Wizard (different practices and often different instruments because yeah ! Instruments are cross-practices too) and her belief could find its roots in the Jewish Kabbalah or in Taoism. And an Alchemist or a wizard could have either belief. Reasons behind the practices would be different (one would use the divine essence of creation while the other would use a sort of body-spirit cultivation. The five agents of the body from Eastern culture being different from the divine essences of western alchemy). And it's only an other example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T11:55:11-08:00","id":1173272,"title":"","content":"Just to clarify: I'm pretty sure that when NicoTheDuck says \u201cbelief\u201d, that's not \u201cBelief\u201d as in \u201cParadigm\u201d, the first formal component of M20's Focus. Likewise, I don't think that he (she?) is using \u201cpractice\u201d to mean \u201cPractice\u201d, the second component of M20's Focus. He's using \u201cbelief\u201d and \u201cpractice\u201d more informally.<br /> <br /> That said, part of the point is that the M20 Focus write-ups for the various factions are rather informal, too; but that's not the same as saying that there's no \u201cthere\u201d there, and that one's choice of Focus and one's choice of faction don't have anything to do with each other. Let's not fall into the fallacy of the excluded middle: just because M20 doesn't insist that everyone in a given faction have precisely the same Focus, that doesn't mean that the opposite is true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T13:43:15-08:00","id":1173309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1173266#post1173266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just throwing this out there\u2026 The Batini cannot have Entropy. It's not \u201cEntropy is rare in their ranks\u201d the way Dimensional Science is rare in Iteration X's ranks; it's a flat-out prohibition.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was actually retconned in revised edition as just being a thing a handful of fanatics did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T13:51:18-08:00","id":1173313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1173309#post1173309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That was actually retconned in revised edition as just being a thing a handful of fanatics did.</div> </div> </div> </div>I got this directly out of M20.<br /> <div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> Despite their mystic acumen, Batini cannot learn the Entropy Arts at all.<br /> \u2014last paragraph, p.203</div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 01-04-2018, 04:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T13:59:51-08:00","id":1173318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1173253#post1173253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am less interested in the &quot;purity of belief&quot; with regard to a specific culture's folkways (except where that's relevant, see above for Disparates) than I am in seeing some actual hard crunchy-style evidence of SECT culture that represents a group-think about the way in which that particular sect does magic that both binds it together and differentiates it from other sects. Though that is implied to some degree, it is an implication that doesn't really manifest currently, and, in fact, the weight of current trends is in the opposing direction.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm still waiting for any solid argument on how any previous edition of modern day Mage has this &quot;hard crunchy-style evidence,&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> What feels weird to me in all this, is that you're still arguing that M20 has &quot;changed&quot; something instead of M20 doing what Mage as always done: leave such things to the people playing the game to bring to life in descriptions instead of &quot;hard crunch.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T14:44:29-08:00","id":1173336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1173318#post1173318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still waiting for any solid argument on how any previous edition of modern day Mage has this &quot;hard crunchy-style evidence,&quot; thing.<br /> What feels weird to me in all this, is that you're still arguing that M20 has &quot;changed&quot; something instead of M20 doing what Mage as always done: leave such things to the people playing the game to bring to life in descriptions instead of &quot;hard crunch.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The old foci system was pretty rigid. Associating one instrument to a Sphere was not really justified. The new Belief/Practice/Instrument system brings flexibility and more roleplay. In a way, it makes the whole thing more &quot;realistic&quot;, or you could say more natural. Concerning the whole thing about chosing the particular instruments. I agree with you, that freedom existed in the previous editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T16:22:09-08:00","id":1173361,"title":"","content":"But you could still pick whatever foci you wanted. Traditions didn't have a list of tools they had to use. Just like M20, we just had a general set of suggestions. A technology focused Hermetic from House Fortunae might have the same foci as a Virtual Adept.... which Ajax is saying means there's no difference between between Hermetics or VAs besides social grouping. The closest things we ever see to what Ajax is talking about were not part of the Paradigm/Focus systems, they were things like the Akashics having Do, or Hypertech being limited to the Technocracy and defector groups... which is something M20 maintained about as well as possible with balancing between different edition variations.<br /> <br /> Dark Ages: Mage is the only book in the line that can really be said to fit Ajax's stated criteria, and it's the outlier, not that standard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T17:21:31-08:00","id":1173377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1173313#post1173313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I got this directly out of M20.<br /> <div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> Despite their mystic acumen, Batini cannot learn the Entropy Arts at all.<br /> \u2014last paragraph, p.203</div></div> </div> </div> </div>Thats ... &quot;unfortunate&quot; is about the most polite word I can think of for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T18:16:39-08:00","id":1173390,"title":"","content":"Agreed; and I personally ignore it (just like I ignore the bit about the Order of Hermes mandating study of Forces). But it <i>is</i> evidence of a M20 group being more than just a socio-political thing, and having some actual mystical weight to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T18:47:43-08:00","id":1173395,"title":"","content":"If evidence of anything, I'd say it's of writers not doing proper research. <br /> <br /> At this point, I'd not be shocked to hear that M20 says that the Dreamspeakers are best friends with were beasts, the Verbena still hang out with vampires all the time and the Euthanatos are all automatically Wyrm-tainted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T08:01:32-08:00","id":1173489,"title":"","content":"Rather than &quot;mystic weight&quot;, I'd say &quot;baggage of paradigm&quot;. I read the Entropy prohibition as something more like, &quot;As the Batini paradigm is so focused on the unity of all people, places, and things, those following this paradigm are unable to conceive of Effects that degrade those things to their component parts. These Effects are most often based in the Entropy sphere. A Batini who wishes to create such Effects must amalgamate their Tradition's paradigm with another which is more accepting of these possibilities - for example, they might take the Dual Tradition merit.&quot; <br /> <br /> To transpose in some DA:M terminology: while the Traditions have created a shared set of &quot;Pillars&quot; for all to use, each paradigm still has a Foundation underlying it. The Foundation used by the Batini denies the entropic end of all things such that an effect exploiting that entropy cannot be based in that Foundation.<br /> <br /> As for whether you believe it makes sense to have this concept for the Ahl-i-Batin or not, your mileage may vary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T09:40:38-08:00","id":1173509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1173318#post1173318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm still waiting for any solid argument on how any previous edition of modern day Mage has this &quot;hard crunchy-style evidence,&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> What feels weird to me in all this, is that you're still arguing that M20 has &quot;changed&quot; something instead of M20 doing what Mage as always done: leave such things to the people playing the game to bring to life in descriptions instead of &quot;hard crunch.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> First edition Mage: The description of Focus where it was tied to a specific material object per Sphere for each Tradition. The legacy of which is things like &quot;personalized focus/instrument&quot;<br /> Second and Revised: Written in throughout whenever the way in which a specific Sect does magic &quot;their&quot; was as opposed to the way other Sects do theirs. This was a particular concern of the Tradition books (to no small degree the first edition books, but expanded heavily and effectively the focus of an entire chapter with mentions and nods throughout the books). <br /> Dark Ages Mage: The essence of the Foundation/Pillar system effectively hard-wiring the way in which each group perceives and casts magic at the fundamental level.<br /> <br /> Sure, mage leaves EVERYTHING to the group. Then goes about explaining exactly how to do things to a large degree, which includes how magic works in the rules and how it is manifests to the characters in the setting. Rules you CAN toss, but, to a degree, if you do, you either have to &quot;go 100% Orphan&quot; (the Brucato Way... which was somewhat hard before the advent of Focus in M20, but doable), have your mage game become idiosyncratic enough that it starts moving outwards to a personalized home version or make it a &quot;rules on the table&quot; game where players say things like &quot;I use Forces 3/Mind 3 to turn all the darkness into love....&quot; with little to no attempt to have casting be anything other than an exercise in rule application. <br /> <br /> In fact, the new Focus rules removes a significant chunk of some of that &quot;bring to life in descriptions&quot; as being &quot;[left]... to the people playing the game&quot; by introducing a fair amount of crunch. Which is definitely something that M20 has &quot;changed&quot;. IMO, probably to the good, as it seems to date in the games we've run with it, that people are getting a better handle on describing the actions their characters are taking casting more robustly and interestingly than they have before, but YMMV. <br /> <br /> The gist of what I am saying is that, before M20 Focus, there was a dearth of advice on how to do the exact thing that the M20 Focus rules explicitly do. The whole &quot;people playing the game.. bring to life [the magic] in descriptions.&quot; Not that it wasn't something that wasn't an issue that was wrestled with regularly, it was just never handled (past the odious, but understandable, first edition this -Sphere-to-this-thingee) other than mostly by fluff. (With the exception of Do, which was handled in effectively the opposite direction to the point it was extracted from the magic rules entirely). However, that fluff was actually describing something actual if not really manifested in the crunch to any significant degree. And that the current rules of Focus are ;largely pulling towards individualized philosophy and practice of magic and more away than toward any sort of Sect-based philosophy and practice of magic. Moreover, this isn't MY idea or an artifact of my understanding of the game. It's something that was specifically addressed by the author/editor in the decisions he made in creating the new rules. It's a change and s deliberate one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T14:08:12-08:00","id":1173575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1173509#post1173509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First edition Mage: The description of Focus where it was tied to a specific material object per Sphere for each Tradition. The legacy of which is things like &quot;personalized focus/instrument&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the legacy of that is actually the &quot;tradition standard&quot; foci where it was assumed that members of a Tradition could use foci that make sense to their Tradition for zero bonus, while personal and unique foci that provided mechanical benefits were added to this.<br /> <br /> In other words, M20 didn't do this. 2e did this and Rev went farther, by putting personal foci over the foci learned by being part of a Tradition. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Second and Revised: Written in throughout whenever the way in which a specific Sect does magic &quot;their&quot; was as opposed to the way other Sects do theirs. </div> </div> </div>So zero &quot;hard crunchy style&quot; stuff. Just lore descriptions we were expected to enact in play.<br /> <br /> [quote]Dark Ages Mage[/quote<br /> <br /> Fails to meet the criteria of the post you're responding to. Again, DAM is a significant outlier to the rest of the Mage, so it isn't evidence of M20 making a significant change here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sure, mage leaves EVERYTHING to the group. </div> </div> </div>Well no, it doesn't. But importantly, it doesn't mechanize the majority of how a Tradition/etc. impacts your character's magical practice and leaves that to the group.. which you're claiming wasn't true until M20 somehow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ,,, &quot;go 100% Orphan&quot; (the Brucato Way... which was somewhat hard before the advent of Focus in M20, but doable),,, </div> </div> </div>Being an Orphan before M20 involved... not having a favored Sphere. Building an Orphan required a bit more thought since you didn't have a Tradition/etc. to fall back on for filling various gaps, but it was never hard, because it has almost no mechanical impact, and the Traditions/etc. have always been so large and vague that &quot;making it up yourself&quot; vs. &quot;picking from a dozen option inside the Tradition,&quot; is more a personal preference than a design issue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In fact, the new Focus rules removes a significant chunk of some of that &quot;bring to life in descriptions&quot; as being &quot;[left]... to the people playing the game&quot; by introducing a fair amount of crunch. </div> </div> </div>I'm starting to think we have very different understandings of the word &quot;crunch&quot; here. Crunch is the mechanical side of the rules, not everything used to define a character in regards to the setting. Picking your character's Avatar Essence isn't a crunch thing, it's a lore thing. It's character defining into the setting, not the rules.<br /> <br /> The M20 Focus system added no new amount of crunch. It modified a bit of crunch (how Intruments work) but the quantity is the same. Having a common set of Paradigms and Practices to pick from to help describe your character isn't crunch, because it doesn't actually interact with any mechanical rules. They're a way to help players' descriptions by clarifying existing setting concepts, not a change to the resolution of magic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which is definitely something that M20 has &quot;changed&quot;. IMO, probably to the good, as it seems to date in the games we've run with it, that people are getting a better handle on describing the actions their characters are taking casting more robustly and interestingly than they have before, but YMMV. </div> </div> </div>No disagreement that the new Focus method is vastly superior for getting people to describe things more vibrantly. Creating a common language for it helped a lot, as did finally getting away from the &quot;one instrument per Sphere&quot; thing since it was always restrictive on descriptions compared to having a selection of personal instruments that you use as makes sense tot he magic you're doing. Even if instruments were more heavily regulated by Traditions, not liking them to Spheres is a good idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And that the current rules of Focus are ;largely pulling towards individualized philosophy and practice of magic and more away than toward any sort of Sect-based philosophy and practice of magic. Moreover, this isn't MY idea or an artifact of my understanding of the game. It's something that was specifically addressed by the author/editor in the decisions he made in creating the new rules. It's a change and s deliberate one. </div> </div> </div>See, I don't think that's what Brucato meant in that. The goal is not to &quot;pull&quot; the game in a particular direction, but make the game more playable to different play-styles. Making personalized magic focused Orphan games more fun doesn't mean Tradition-style focused games suffer in M20. It's just - as it as pretty much always been - how the group wants to do things.<br /> <br /> If you want more of a group focused game in M20, you don't need to change anything. You just need to be selective with how players construct their Focuses to make sure they mesh well with their sect.<br /> <br /> Basically, I don't see this &quot;zero sum game of personal magic vs group method magic&quot; argument as baring out. You could make very personalized mages in previous editions, the game simply didn't do you any favors by lacking a common language and then only introducing group specific language for talking about it. M20 added common language. That's all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T17:09:49-08:00","id":1173625,"title":"","content":"In 2e and Revised, the lists of suggested Instruments were provided directly by the metaphysical sect write-ups, and the closest you got to Paradigm and Practice were, again, the sect write-ups. If your mage didn't join a sect, she not only didn't have an affinity Sphere; you also didn't have any guidance on how her magick worked. M20 reorganized this by providing lists of sample Paradigms and Practices, having the Practices provide the lists of associated Instruments (and Abilities, BTW; that's new crunch IMHO), and having the sect write-ups list likely Paradigms and Practices. <br /> <br /> Heavy Arms is right in that the <i>Focus</i> sections for each sect in M20 are equivalent to the <i>Philosophy</i> and <i>Style</i> sections in 2e and the <i>Philosophy</i> and <i>Theories and Practices</i> sections in Revised, just phrased in a way that utilizes the Paradigm and Practice write-ups provided later in the book. This gives the M20 sect Focus write-ups a more modular feel than their predecessor counterparts, but doesn't really make them any more or less flexible in terms of determining how a member's magick works. This is spelled out in <b>Book of Secrets</b> (<i>the Role of Culture</i>, pp.168\u2013169):<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">\u201cThe <b>Focus</b> entry on each two-page spread of <b>Mage 20</b> describes the preferred focus of the metaphysical society in question, and although certain individual variations are allowed \u2014 say, a Verbena witch using a computer \u2014 members of that society employ most, if not all, of the focus elements mentioned within that entry.\u201d</div><br /> On the other hand, the reorganization means that you always have guidance for how one's magick works; because you always know that mage's Paradigm and Practices. This is true whether or not he has joined a metaphysical sect \u2014 although your choice of sect <i>does</i> guide your choice of Focus. What was previously an Orphan or Hollow One who had an eclectic style patched together from a mishmash of magical beliefs (and little guidance for the player) is now a mage with the Practice of Gutter Magick. The big change here is that M20 doesn't carry the assumption that Orphans primarily practice Gutter Magick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 01-06-2018, 01:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-06T04:24:18-08:00","id":1173728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1173625#post1173625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the reorganization means that you always have guidance for how one's magick works</div> </div> </div> </div>According to my experience, this is gold. I play Mage in campaigns, but also in one-shot sessions during conventions or with friends. And for players who do not know the game well (or at all), this guidance helps me a lot. When they want to do something, I always ask these questions :<br /> - How do you do it ? (or With what do you do it ?)<br /> - Why do you think you can do it ? (or What in your belief allows you to do it ?)<br /> If they cannot answer those questions, it appears that they cannot perform their magick the way they wanted it. Then, I let them precise/correct their action so that their magick functions in their paradigm. With time (especially in campagins), this brought much more commitment in the game from the players and all descriptions of Magick feats improved significantly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1173625#post1173625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The big change here is that M20 doesn't carry the assumption that Orphans primarily practice Gutter Magick.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. And I like that point. That's not because you're a self taught Mage that you pratice gutter magick. Even self-taught, a Mage is still part of culture and still believes en something.<br /> <br /> It also almost definitely destroyed the purple paradigm. Since I disliked it (not in the game's spirit in my opinion), this a good point too <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-06T10:39:26-08:00","id":1173787,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Heavy Arms;n1173575]<br /> <br /> Well, the legacy of that is actually the &quot;tradition standard&quot; foci where it was assumed that members of a Tradition could use foci that make sense to their Tradition for zero bonus, while personal and unique foci that provided mechanical benefits were added to this.<br /> <br /> In other words, M20 didn't do this. 2e did this and Rev went farther, by putting personal foci over the foci learned by being part of a Tradition.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So zero &quot;hard crunchy style&quot; stuff. Just lore descriptions we were expected to enact in play.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dark Ages Mage[/quote<br /> <br /> Fails to meet the criteria of the post you're responding to. Again, DAM is a significant outlier to the rest of the Mage, so it isn't evidence of M20 making a significant change here.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Well no, it doesn't. But importantly, it doesn't mechanize the majority of how a Tradition/etc. impacts your character's magical practice and leaves that to the group.. which you're claiming wasn't true until M20 somehow.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Being an Orphan before M20 involved... not having a favored Sphere. Building an Orphan required a bit more thought since you didn't have a Tradition/etc. to fall back on for filling various gaps, but it was never hard, because it has almost no mechanical impact, and the Traditions/etc. have always been so large and vague that &quot;making it up yourself&quot; vs. &quot;picking from a dozen option inside the Tradition,&quot; is more a personal preference than a design issue.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm starting to think we have very different understandings of the word &quot;crunch&quot; here. Crunch is the mechanical side of the rules, not everything used to define a character in regards to the setting. Picking your character's Avatar Essence isn't a crunch thing, it's a lore thing. It's character defining into the setting, not the rules.<br /> <br /> The M20 Focus system added no new amount of crunch. It modified a bit of crunch (how Intruments work) but the quantity is the same. Having a common set of Paradigms and Practices to pick from to help describe your character isn't crunch, because it doesn't actually interact with any mechanical rules. They're a way to help players' descriptions by clarifying existing setting concepts, not a change to the resolution of magic.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> No disagreement that the new Focus method is vastly superior for getting people to describe things more vibrantly. Creating a common language for it helped a lot, as did finally getting away from the &quot;one instrument per Sphere&quot; thing since it was always restrictive on descriptions compared to having a selection of personal instruments that you use as makes sense tot he magic you're doing. Even if instruments were more heavily regulated by Traditions, not liking them to Spheres is a good idea.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> See, I don't think that's what Brucato meant in that. The goal is not to &quot;pull&quot; the game in a particular direction, but make the game more playable to different play-styles. Making personalized magic focused Orphan games more fun doesn't mean Tradition-style focused games suffer in M20. It's just - as it as pretty much always been - how the group wants to do things.<br /> <br /> If you want more of a group focused game in M20, you don't need to change anything. You just need to be selective with how players construct their Focuses to make sure they mesh well with their sect.<br /> <br /> Basically, I don't see this &quot;zero sum game of personal magic vs group method magic&quot; argument as baring out. You could make very personalized mages in previous editions, the game simply didn't do you any favors by lacking a common language and then only introducing group specific language for talking about it. M20 added common language. That's all. </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, I agree that, in some places, we are arguing past each other because we are working from different definition. To me and to my understanding, fluff is JUST the descriptions, e.g. the history stuff, the philosophy stuff, the wordy stuff. Anything that has an effect on roll-playing or even strongly structures role-playing iscrunch. Since the Focus rules say, you must have at least 1 X, at least 1 Y and at least 7 Z, it's crunch. Even it the crunch is designed to set up descriptive elements in game. External examples are available in games like 7th Sea and Fate (and so on) where there are &quot;attributes&quot; that color or reward descriptive play. Also, the stunt system from Exalted and Scion is in the same vein. To stunt, you must describe and then you get an effect that has a rules effect. Sure, Focus is less intrusive to roll-playing in places. Belief and Practice are pretty fluffy, but Instruments are or can be, much more effective on the crunch side, even if they also have a high &quot;fluff&quot; content. <br /> <br /> I disagree that DA is not acceptable to bring in. 1) It's a version of Mage and therefore whether or not it's an outlier, that makes it inherently relevant. In fact, it might make it more relevant as a way to compare certain aspects. 2) DA Mage was specifically brought up when these discussions were going on as a model for changes in M20. specifically for the purposes of this discussion, as I described, that most of what is now Focus was hardwired into the Sect (though other aspects of DA were discussed as well, like the Stat + Stat dice pool instead of just using one stat for all magic dice pools). And, in fact, Brucato, who ASKED for this input, was very transparent in the decisions he was making. He specifically stated that he rejected both crunch and fluff and the intersection of the two in favor of exactly what I am saying, a magic system that is based on individualized philosophy and practice irrespective of Sect. Which is manifested heavily in the example characters in BoS. (He also discussed it in terms of his personal occult journey as well.) <br /> <br /> I admit to characterizing that philosophy as &quot;Orphan's First&quot; or the &quot;Brucato Way&quot; but, to a degree that's for ease of discussion. If we know what that means, it's a great shorthand to encompass a concept that take a lot of verbage to describe. I want to go on record and say that it is NOT meant perjoratively. I have noticed one of the difficulties still faces by my very veteran group of Mage players is getting a handle on how MUCH a starting Mage should be capable of. So our next game is going to be an Initiates game and, to further highlight the descriptive aspects of the (sorta) knew Focus system, I am going &quot;full-on Orphan's First&quot; and we're going to be starting the game Pre-Awakening, go through the Awakenings and then the development of individual Practices and selection of Instruments. I'm going to keep the Factions/Sects OUT of the game (they may exist, they may not.... ).<br /> <br /> But, all that being said, I will still maintain that the changes in the M20 rules, specifically in the way in which Focus is handled, formally preferences the idea of individual character's comprehension of magic over that of the idea of a Sect-wide &quot;group-think&quot; that characterizes the magic of each Sect for the most part from all others to the level that it relegates that it to something that doesn't exist past the original level of pure fluff. Yes, that second part was definitely open-ended and vague compared to the codification of current rules (I'd say &quot;crunch&quot; but, obviously, YM does V), but doesn't erase the distinction. Nor does it undermine the way in which it creates a trend in a particular direction that to some degree is going to affect the way the Sects matter in a.... I hesitate to use &quot;negative&quot; but can't think of a better word... way and that leads to some cognitive dissonance when the game definitely LOVES it's intricate war of dueling philosophical reality Illuminati and the rules give that an underlying &quot;meh&quot;. (In fact, it seems likely that a lot of the most difficult parts of HDYDT is a result of some of these issues.) I mean, if it's possible to run an Iteration-X cyborg whose Practice is Dominance, Voodoo and Yoga (all with the appropriate &quot;science-y&quot; gloss) and shies away from having any Instruments that are mechanism-like, then it does make Iteration-X less about machines, because that's not really something that It-X members have to share.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-06T11:33:32-08:00","id":1173799,"title":"","content":"Not all combinations of beliefs/practices/instruments is coherent or logical. Nobody said that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8572,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","user":"NicoTheDuck","date":". 01-06-2018, 02:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-06T11:41:59-08:00","id":1173803,"title":"","content":"There's no such thing as a rules system that's immune to abuse; and M20's Focus system is no exception. Just because you can come up with a combination of Practices and Instruments that conform to the letter of a group's Focus entry while violating its spirit, that doesn't mean that it isn't an outlier or shouldn't be rejected by the Storyteller for violating the spirit of the group in question. If one of my players presented the ItXer you describe, I'd want a convincing explanation from him as to how that concept is appropriate for Iteration X before I allowed it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 01-06-2018, 03:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-06T12:19:27-08:00","id":1173811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1173787#post1173787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me and to my understanding, fluff is JUST the descriptions, e.g. the history stuff, the philosophy stuff, the wordy stuff. Anything that has an effect on roll-playing or even strongly structures role-playing iscrunch.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems like a very expansive definition of crunch compared to most online essays and forum discussions.<br /> <br /> On top of the fact that game designers tend to highly dislike the whole crunch vs. fluff thing (especially the inherently dismissive name of fluff), crunch is generally thought to derive from &quot;number crunching,&quot; as in the part of the game that actually involves manipulating numbers.<br /> <br /> Your definition is hard to work with. Naming a character is crunch in your definition, because names structure role-play, and can even impact rolls (like Correspondence effects in Mage, certain Rites in Werewolf, or just having a name or not for mundane Investigation rolls, etc.). It gets to the point where virtually nothing can actually be not-crunch, unless it's essentially irrelevant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> External examples are available in games like 7th Sea and Fate (and so on) where there are &quot;attributes&quot; that color or reward descriptive play. Also, the stunt system from Exalted and Scion is in the same vein. To stunt, you must describe and then you get an effect that has a rules effect. </div> </div> </div>I'm not getting the connection here. 7the Sea and Fate have specific mechanics around these things. The ability to describe your own Aspects/Skills/Stunts in Fate instead of picking from a set list is freeform, but have distinct mechanical effects. You don't just have &quot;Swashbuckler&quot; as a generic term. If it was an Aspect, you could spend points to get a +2 to a roll where swashbuckling would be a benefit, or get compelled to act more-swashbuckling for fate points. If it's a skill, it will have a +X modifier attached to it for rolls where it applies.<br /> <br /> Stunts in Exalted are, again, a free form thing, but there's criteria for qualifying for one. You don't just get to say, &quot;I round house kick for a level 3 stunt.&quot; Again, there are also distinct mechanics here.<br /> <br /> Paradigm and Practice in M20 don't have mechanics attached to them. There's no +2 on your roll for enacting your Practice, or regaining quintessence by describing how your Paradigm informs your magic in an awesome way.<br /> <br /> Instruments are the only part of Focus that has direct mechanical interactions, but that's always been true in previous editions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I disagree that DA is not acceptable to bring in. </div> </div> </div>Because comparing DAM to M20 makes M20 look more extreme in change, when DAM's mechanics are explicitly something M20 doesn't care about, while Mage 1e-Revised are things M20 cares about. DAM is as irrelevant to the point I'm contesting as Mage: the Awakening, Ars Magica, and Monte Cooke's WOD are. However connected they might all be to the larger &quot;Mage&quot; family of games, they're not what M20 is about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In fact, it might make it more relevant as a way to compare certain aspects. </div> </div> </div>This has nothing to do with your attempt to justify M20 representing a significant change from Mage 1e-Revised in terms of &quot;hard crunch style evidence,&quot; of how much sect based vs. personal based magic is enforced by the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> DA Mage was specifically brought up when these discussions were going on as a model for changes in M20. </div> </div> </div>Which remains an horrible idea. M20 is supposed to be an omnibus edition of Mage the Ascension, not a book for people that wanted a completely different approach to magic that made Ascension so interesting and engaging in the first place: that we didn't need specialized systems where each kind of magic gets it's own subsystem. All magic uses the same systems, and different magic users are a layer of personal beliefs (regardless of if they came from a Tradition or you make them up as an Orphan) on top of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> He specifically stated that he rejected both crunch and fluff and the intersection of the two in favor of exactly what I am saying, a magic system that is based on individualized philosophy and practice irrespective of Sect. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that thing he made sure was already built into the system when he developed Mage 2e. That's my whole point, You keep acting like this stuff is &quot;new&quot; when it isn't. Brucato mage it so individualized philosophy was the primary aspect of magic in Mage back in 2e. M20 includes a more refined and developed version, not something that represents an actual major change.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I admit to characterizing that philosophy as &quot;Orphan's First&quot; or the &quot;Brucato Way&quot; but, to a degree that's for ease of discussion. If we know what that means, it's a great shorthand to encompass a concept that take a lot of verbage to describe. </div> </div> </div>Sorry but this is bullshit. Characterizing things in a fashion that's designed rhetorically to phrase your position as the default correct one is not about ease of discussion. It doesn't make discussion easier, it makes shutting down people disagreeing with you easier, and it makes me think that what you mean with those phrases is, &quot;I, Ajax, am not actually going to engage with anything at might make my point look weak, and will bend anything and everything to make it sound like I'm right.&quot; I don't think you mean it as a pejorative, but I do think you mean it as a dismissive rhetorical device.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But, all that being said, I will still maintain that the changes in the M20 rules, specifically in the way in which Focus is handled, formally preferences the idea of individual character's comprehension of magic over that of the idea of a Sect-wide &quot;group-think&quot; that characterizes the magic of each Sect for the most part from all others to the level that it relegates that it to something that doesn't exist past the original level of pure fluff. </div> </div> </div>Maintain it all you want, just acknowledge you've presented no evidence to this being the case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, if it's possible to run an Iteration-X cyborg whose Practice is Dominance, Voodoo and Yoga (all with the appropriate &quot;science-y&quot; gloss) and shies away from having any Instruments that are mechanism-like, then it does make Iteration-X less about machines, because that's not really something that It-X members have to share. </div> </div> </div>The problem is, I could do this in Revised, so M20 didn't change anything significant. The only thing stopping me in either edition is the ST/other players thinking it's stupid, not the game itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 01-06-2018, 03:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-06T14:05:32-08:00","id":1173835,"title":"","content":"Let me see about being a bit more explicit: M20 shifted some terminology around and rearranged how things are organized; but as Heavy Arms says, the essentials are unchanged:<br /> <br /> \u2022 M20 Focus is M2e/MRev Paradigm. It's a blanket term for the following three elements and the synergy between them.<br /> \u2022 M20 Paradigm is M2e/MRev Philosophy. In all renditions, it is about why you do magick, what you hope to accomplish with it.<br /> \u2022 M20 Practice is M2e Style/MRev Theories &amp; Practices. In all renditions, it guides you in how you use your tools by providing a framework for how you think magick works. <br /> \u2022 M20 Instruments are M2e/MRev Foci. In all renditions, they're the actions and items that you use to work your magick.<br /> <br /> The only real change is that M20 lists sample Paradigms, Abilities, and Instruments in its Practice write-ups, whereas M2e and MRev didn't even <i>have</i> standalone Paradigm or Practice write-ups; only what was in the group write-ups. <br /> <br /> Yes, this makes M20 more about individual magick, as the philosophies, theories, and practices are described outside the context of the groups. But it doesn't do so by weakening or eliminating the various groups' commitment to their philosophies, theories, and practices (in M20 terms, their Focus). Not that that commitment was particularly uniform in the past; the Order of Hermes, for instance, is a lot more of a stickler for a formal education in magick than, say, the Cultists of Ecstasy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 01-07-2018, 06:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-16T08:28:13-08:00","id":1176520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zennis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition#post1167408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Dalou'laoshi/The Elemental Dragons (who according to Sydicate Revied have been largely purged), remnants of the Craft Masons and the Gabrielites/Cabal of Pure Thought as well some others who have formed a new convention within this Tradition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm really glad I listened to my friend and never read any of the convention books. He loves the Technocracy, but hates most of the published material on them.<br /> <br /> They could use some serious development, but I kind of liked the The Dalou'laoshi/The Elemental Dragons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":21481,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","user":"Onkwe","date":". 01-31-2018, 11:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T09:47:33-08:00","id":1182961,"title":"","content":"I read through the whole thread, and didn't realize how much it shifted in subject.<br /> <br /> As for the paradigm, practice, and instrument system, I don't want to say I didn't like it exactly. I still have some hesitations about a few of the paradigm suggestions; some seem more like attitudes than a basic view of how reality works. However that doesn't mean the whole thing needs to be tossed. I realized the practice aspect was basically in the Orphans Survival Guide. I really liked the broad categories they set up to help guide in creating a mage that doesn't come from an established practice. I remember back in the day wishing they would have done something similar for the Traditions, Crafts, and Conventions. So yeah, once it hit me I liked it a lot more. My only remaining beef with the magick system is the sphere bloat. Aside from requiring too many spheres to do much of anything, it really hampers certain styles and paradigms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":21481,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","user":"Onkwe","date":". 02-07-2018, 11:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T10:49:09-08:00","id":1183305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Onkwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1176520#post1176520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm really glad I listened to my friend and never read any of the convention books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I think that's a big big loss.<br /> I love the Technocracy as much as I do the Trads, and the new-old Revised line of Technocracy Conventionbooks is really good, in my opinion. There might be some pieces one dislikes, but that's the case with any writeup, usually.<br /> Together with Guide To The Technocracy, I think they are - all things considered - the only writeups that actually give the Technocracy even a chance of voicing their side of things, over the more Tradition-biased side of things in the other books.<br /> With M20 being an exception, as it's the first corebook to actually be relatively neutral - in the way that it switches back and forth between the individual viewpoints.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 02-07-2018, 01:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T21:18:48-08:00","id":1183471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Onkwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1176520#post1176520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They could use some serious development, but I kind of liked the The Dalou'laoshi/The Elemental Dragons.</div> </div> </div> </div>For what it's worth, it looks like <b>Technocracy Reloaded</b> is going to be ignoring that part of the Revised Convention Books: instead of trying to fold the Elemental Dragons into the original five Conventions, it's apparently going to push the opposite direction and introduce even more non-western Technocracies \u2014 at the very least, an African one. And I'm pretty sure the Elemental Dragons will be getting more attention, too. <br /> <br /> And then there's <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/992558-shard-the-technocratic-civil-war\">New Avalon</a>\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-08-2018, 01:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-08T11:17:43-08:00","id":1183640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1183471#post1183471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For what it's worth, it looks like <b>Technocracy Reloaded</b> is going to be ignoring that part of the Revised Convention Books: instead of trying to fold the Elemental Dragons into the original five Conventions, it's apparently going to push the opposite direction and introduce even more non-western Technocracies \u2014 at the very least, an African one. And I'm pretty sure the Elemental Dragons will be getting more attention, too.<br /> <br /> And then there's <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/992558-shard-the-technocratic-civil-war\">New Avalon</a>\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Where did you get the info about the Technocracy Reloaded? <br /> <br /> Because if what you said is true, that's pretty cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-08T11:22:30-08:00","id":1183641,"title":"","content":"Phil Brucato, during the M20 Kickstarter when the Technocracy Reloaded stretch goal was announced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-08T15:37:55-08:00","id":1183733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1183305#post1183305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally, I think that's a big big loss.<br /> I love the Technocracy as much as I do the Trads, and the new-old Revised line of Technocracy Conventionbooks is really good, in my opinion. There might be some pieces one dislikes, but that's the case with any writeup, usually.<br /> Together with Guide To The Technocracy, I think they are - all things considered - the only writeups that actually give the Technocracy even a chance of voicing their side of things, over the more Tradition-biased side of things in the other books.<br /> With M20 being an exception, as it's the first corebook to actually be relatively neutral - in the way that it switches back and forth between the individual viewpoints.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've never cared for most of the Tradition books either, from either edition. I usually got more from a google search or heading over to the library than I ever got out of most of them. So I doubt I would have gotten much out of the Convention books either. I prefer the Technocracy in my head anyways, lol.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1183471#post1183471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For what it's worth, it looks like <b>Technocracy Reloaded</b> is going to be ignoring that part of the Revised Convention Books: instead of trying to fold the Elemental Dragons into the original five Conventions, it's apparently going to push the opposite direction and introduce even more non-western Technocracies \u2014 at the very least, an African one. And I'm pretty sure the Elemental Dragons will be getting more attention, too.<br /> <br /> And then there's <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/992558-shard-the-technocratic-civil-war\">New Avalon</a>\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes sense. Revised wanted to get rid of all the extra groups, and really expand on the idea of the Traditions being big tent organizations; diversifying the entities within. Meanwhile Brucato, being more in favor of the orphan POV, seems to favor lots of independent groups of the four main factions.<br /> <br /> Still Africa getting some coverage is a major step in the right direction. Reminds me of a homebrew expansion of the Virtual Adept defection involving a lot of '3rd world' Technocrats joining them. They felt stifled by being dominated by the European old boys club nature of the Technocracy, and helped in ending colonization over their homelands. However, despite good intentions, they also helped unleash the horrors of neo-colonialism, destructive reforms to modernize, and the various stripes of fanaticism that characterized that tragic period of history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":21481,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","user":"Onkwe","date":". 02-08-2018, 06:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-08T19:06:07-08:00","id":1183796,"title":"","content":"I'm in favor of a lot of culturally diverse factions of disparates, and Trad sub-groups, but since Globalism is a central part of the Union's identity and themes, I'd rather they not have that kind of cultural division. It would seem to under,mine the point. Yes that means the Union in Africa and Asia have a perspective some would see as inherently Western, but that\u2019s because they're rooted in Western Imperialism turned neo-Imperialism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 02-08-2018, 10:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-08T19:49:12-08:00","id":1183803,"title":"","content":"The good news is that you're free to ignore them and just say that the Victorian-based Technocracy is the only one still around. Meanwhile, those of us who prefer a more nuanced take have the African and Asian Technocracies to play with, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-08T23:21:48-08:00","id":1183844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1183803#post1183803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The good news is that you're free to ignore them and just say that the Victorian-based Technocracy is the only one still around. Meanwhile, those of us who prefer a more nuanced take have the African and Asian Technocracies to play with, too.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well yes obviously, that's always true. But unless we're going to start arguing there shouldn't be a canon at all, and every book should just be a toolkit book rather than presenting a consistent setting, I think discussions about the relative pluses and minuses of different creative decisions and how the zero-sum game of wordcount in spent is still allowed.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't throw the Five Elemental Dragons out entirely. The Dalou'laoshi and the Courts of Chrysanthemums and Plum Blossoms obviously have deep roots going back to before Western empires spanned the globe. But in the modern age, I'd leave them within the Conventions of the broader Technocratic Union. The members of Zi Guang are Progenitors at risk of being labeled &quot;reality deviants&quot; by their fellow Technocrats (including those of Chinese ancestry with less traditionalist bent to their paradigm). The Saensaeng are the only one that don't fit in the broader Union as far as I can tell, but then it never made a lot of sense why a bunch of Bushido Shinto mystics aligned themselves with Chinese artisans either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T05:29:12-08:00","id":1183897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1167408-replacing-the-virtual-adepts-and-the-etherites-with-another-tradition?p=1183844#post1183844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well yes obviously, that's always true. But unless we're going to start arguing there shouldn't be a canon at all, and every book should just be a toolkit book rather than presenting a consistent setting, I think discussions about the relative pluses and minuses of different creative decisions and how the zero-sum game of wordcount in spent is still allowed.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't throw the Five Elemental Dragons out entirely. The Dalou'laoshi and the Courts of Chrysanthemums and Plum Blossoms obviously have deep roots going back to before Western empires spanned the globe. But in the modern age, I'd leave them within the Conventions of the broader Technocratic Union. The members of Zi Guang are Progenitors at risk of being labeled &quot;reality deviants&quot; by their fellow Technocrats (including those of Chinese ancestry with less traditionalist bent to their paradigm). The Saensaeng are the only one that don't fit in the broader Union as far as I can tell, but then it never made a lot of sense why a bunch of Bushido Shinto mystics aligned themselves with Chinese artisans either.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's going to be more of a regionalized faction that is still comprised of the five conventions than new conventions or another secretive conspiracy like the Dragons. I swear I remember something about mages representing an African trade league joining the Convention of the White Tower, back when the Order of Reason was first formed. So there's that.<br /> <br /> I do understand how you feel, since the Technocracy's conventions, to me at least, should be looked at as five facets of a unified paradigm than the sharp divisions that mark the Traditions, just with tech. And I like the Dragons more as a heavily regionalized faction within the Technocracy than the quasi-mystics of canon. I can see there might be a greater tolerance for mystic interpretations of things, but for the most part they are Technomancers. And they haven't blended completely in because the Union is still dominated by its European founders, and ignores the issues as &quot;latent nationalism&quot; than not welcoming the Dragons in as equal partners, despite being older organizations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":21481,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","user":"Onkwe","date":". 02-09-2018, 09:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}